WEBVTT

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:43.120
KITANOSAWA VILLAGE

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:17.470
Now then, Tokyo Governor, Asakura...Would you please deliver your address?

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:24.140
To my fellow thirteen million Tokyo citizens...

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:28.020
And to all railway line enthusiasts across the nation...

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:30.520
Thank you for your patience.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:35.690
The operation of the Metropolitan Subway Line No.15-the Touto Line-is now underway!

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:39.360
A threatening letter!? To the Governor!?

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:43.830
This was delivered to the Asakura residence yesterday afternoon.

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:46.040
There was no return address on it.

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:54.000
"By the haughty and arrogant means you've operated your 4-year Tokyo administration..."Divine punishment shall ensue"

00:02:54.380 --> 00:03:00.930
Haughty and arrogant? Hasn't Asakura and the first term of his administration been highly regarded?

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:04.050
Well, people have different feelings and opinions.

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:08.600
There are no doubt dissatisfied and enraged people motivated by irrational beliefs.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:12.190
It's as Shiratori-kun has said.

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:16.570
Tomorrow, Mr. Asakura is scheduled to attend the Touto Line opening ceremony.

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:20.360
We've been assigned the task of guarding the governor.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.320
Do not let your guard down any under circumstances.

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:45.800
The governor has now boarded the train.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:53.690
I'm really excited! About this "Big Universe Exhibition"!

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:56.360
I heard they have spaceship simulation!

00:03:56.860 --> 00:03:58.940
Ayumi wants to give it a try!

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:02.320
But, it seems a certain someone is preoccupied with something else.

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:04.320
You're intrigued, then?

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:07.160
About what Mouri-kun heard from inspector Megure...

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:09.620
The threatening letter addressed to the governor.

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:12.710
yeah, I really hope nothing comes of it.

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:39.610
We're about to enter the Shin-Yamate Tunnel.

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:46.370
That reminds me, this tunnel...

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:50.700
It'll run alongside the Touto Line!

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:53.160
They Run parallel for about a kilometer.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:57.420
That's the curve.

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:00.550
After taking this curve, we'll be at the Touto Line Junction.

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:11.390
What's wrong, Conan-kun?

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:12.430
Nothing...

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:15.940
Who was that shadow just now?

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:19.770
That was a stopping area, but I didn't see a parked car or motorbike...

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:22.030
They were also holding something in their hand...

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:31.450
Don't tell me!

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:35.790
Professor! Stop the car!

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:36.920
What?

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:40.130
Bombs! Someone's planted bombs in the tunnel!!

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:41.880
Bombs!?

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:43.050
did you say bombs!?

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:46.510
But...

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:49.680
I can't until we reach the next stopping area!

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:08.780
Conan-kun!

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:47.280
They've activated the detonator!?

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:49.820
Damn!

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:11.760
Megure here.

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:12.760
This is Kudou!

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:15.430
Hurry and stop the train at once!

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:17.520
There are bombs about to blow!

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:18.560
Bombs!?

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:20.140
Takagi-kun!

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:25.230
Stop the train!

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:26.150
There are bombs!

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:11.360
It really hurts ...

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:13.700
An earthquake?

00:08:13.990 --> 00:08:15.240
No, that's not it!

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:22.830
The train's coming out!

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:24.880
That's the Touto Line!

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:26.670
Kudou-kun!

00:08:27.170 --> 00:08:29.960
This is bad! If I recall, there's a curve up ahead!

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:45.600
Stop!

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:47.150
Stop!

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:49.150
Stop!

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:53.280
Stop!

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:10.130
We're saved...

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:13.760
Mr. Governor! Are you hurt?

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:17.300
I'm all right... Thank you!

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:52.050
I'm high school detective, Kudou Shinichi.

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:56.340
While visiting an amusement park with my childhood friend and classmate, Mouri ran...

00:09:56.550 --> 00:10:00.300
I witnessed a man in black in the midst of a suspicious transaction.

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:03.220
While caught up in watching the deal...

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:06.390
I failed to notice his partner coming up behind me.

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:11.060
Those men forced me to swallow poison...

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:12.440
And when I came to...

00:10:13.190 --> 00:10:15.280
My body had shrunk.

00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:18.200
If those guys found out that Kudou Shinichi was still alive...

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:22.080
They'd come after me again...And put those around me at risk.

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:27.000
At Professor Agasa's suggestion, I decided to conceal my true identity.

00:10:27.010 --> 00:10:29.370
When Ran asked for my name, in that instant...I become Edogawa Conan.

00:10:29.880 --> 00:10:31.670
In order to obtain information on those guys...

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:34.710
I went to live with Ran, whose father is a private detective.

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:39.090
These Kids are my current classmates...

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:40.590
Genta.

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:41.600
Mitsuhiko.

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:42.350
Ayumi.

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:47.430
They formed the "Detective Boys" and force me to join.

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:51.520
And...This is old man Mouri Kogorou.

00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:59.320
Need I explain more?

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:02.740
These two device are inventions of Professor Agasa.

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:07.540
THe professor has come up with unique devices one after the other, all tailor-made for me in my shrunken form.

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:12.290
The Anywhere Ball Dispersing Belt...

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:15.710
Pressing a button on the buckle inflates a soccer ball and ejects it--a nifty invention.

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:20.470
And the spotlight this time around is on this high performance snowboard.

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:24.470
Stepping on the acceleration pedal enables autocruise even when not on a slope.

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:28.140
Of course, like my skateboard, it has a turbo engine.

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:32.440
BY the way, as for those who know my true identity...

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:34.400
There's someone other than the professor.

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:37.690
Haibara Ai. Her real name is Miyano Shino.

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:41.570
She was originally a member of the Black Organization, but...

00:11:41.910 --> 00:11:45.080
Following a certain incident, she decided to take her own life...

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:48.950
Snd took the same drug I was forced to, but her body ended up shrinking instead.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:53.330
As such, with addiction of Haibara who now lives with the professor...

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:57.000
We set out on our newfound lives as first graders.

00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:01.220
Even though I've become smaller, my mind remains the same.

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:03.430
The unbeaten great detective...

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:08.060
There is only one truth!

00:12:12.310 --> 00:12:15.110
What the perpetrator utilized were plastic explosives.

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:20.150
The mechanism was set up in a way that enabled the timer to be engaged via remote control

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:21.860
Regarding the timer...

00:12:21.990 --> 00:12:25.120
According to Edogawa Conan-kun, who witnessed the culprit...

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:31.500
After confirming the train had passed overhead, they pressed the switch on thier remote

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:34.630
The train was traveling at 60 kilometers per hour

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:39.460
The distance from the stopping area where the culprit was seen to the bombs was 250 meters

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:44.590
As a result, our calculation suggest the timer was likely set to 15 seconds

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:48.220
Had the driver not applied the brakes immediately,

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:53.600
the train would have entered the blast radius...Which would have no doubt ended in dire tragedy.

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:59.610
Inspector Megure, who was the person that called your cell phone and ordered the train be stopped?

00:12:59.690 --> 00:13:01.490
That was...

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:06.370
A certain police assistant. That's all we can say.

00:13:06.620 --> 00:13:10.830
At any rate including Governor Asakura...No passengers on board were injured.

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:16.790
Inspector...As always, I request my involvement remain confidential.

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:20.670
Due to my line of work, I'd prefer to not increase my number of enemies.

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:24.090
His "line of work"? Isn't he just a high school student?

00:13:24.550 --> 00:13:26.720
And, thanks to that young boy, Conan..

00:13:26.970 --> 00:13:30.560
The fact that the number of vehicles damaged by the explosion remained zero...

00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:33.020
Was indeed nothing but a miracle.

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:37.770
This Edogawa Conan-kun...How come he noticed the bombs?

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:40.610
That's because this Mouri Kogorou sitting right next to me...

00:13:40.690 --> 00:13:44.320
Mentioned to him that the perpetrator might utilize explosives to carry out their crime.

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:47.610
As expected of Great Detective Mouri!

00:13:48.070 --> 00:13:51.030
Did I say something like that?

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:54.250
Mouri-san, can you share with us any comment regarding the culprit?

00:13:57.370 --> 00:14:01.250
Their crime carried out with the purpose of claiming Governor Asakura's life...

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:04.800
As well as sabotaging one of the highlights of his second term in the new metropolitan subway line...

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:10.390
Will never be tolerated!!

00:14:10.510 --> 00:14:13.220
Is anything already known at this point regarding the culprit?

00:14:14.020 --> 00:14:18.190
Unfortunately, the security camera installed in the tunnel

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:20.270
did not capture footage of the aforementioned stopping area.

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:23.570
Moreover, the culprit likely used the emergency exit and nearby slope...

00:14:23.690 --> 00:14:27.030
In order to escape to the main highway from the ground level.

00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:30.450
But, as of now, no known witnesses can confirm that.

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:36.500
Conan-kun also said he couldn't tell the culprit's face, age, or gender.

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:41.380
We police consider this a crime against Governor Asakura's 4-year Tokyo administration...

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:45.590
Motivated by one-sided dissatisfaction and hatred.

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:47.930
Our investigation is focusing on that angle.

00:14:48.130 --> 00:14:49.050
That will be all.

00:14:51.850 --> 00:14:55.140
This had been a live broadcast from the press conference held at police headquarters.

00:14:56.730 --> 00:14:58.690
What, so that's it?

00:14:58.850 --> 00:15:02.690
They didn't even say a word about us Detective Boys, did they?

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:04.150
How boring!

00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:07.030
All right, lets's play a game! A game!

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:08.780
Good idea.

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:15.540
Looks like the search for the culprit is rough going.

00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:17.830
That threatening letter...

00:15:18.210 --> 00:15:22.130
Isn't it possible it was just camouflage intended to hide the culprit's true motive for the crime?

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:24.500
huh? camouflage?

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:25.840
Say, Professor...

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:30.630
Wasn't Governor Asakura once the Minister of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism?

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:33.180
During his term as minister,

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:37.520
didn't he tear down a village in Niigata in order to build a dam?

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:42.440
Oh, I remember that. If I recall correctly, it's the Kitanosawa Dam.

00:15:43.520 --> 00:15:47.730
Back then, Minister Asakura went to the village himself...

00:15:48.070 --> 00:15:52.240
Along with plenty of security money and nice replacement land offer.

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:57.040
He stayed in the village for a week...Engaged every villager in intense, personal conversation...

00:15:57.240 --> 00:16:01.210
And received their near-unanimous approval after gaining their trust.

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:05.210
Then, after taking only three years to build the new village...

00:16:05.590 --> 00:16:08.630
And requiring an unprecedented record of just five years to construct the dam,

00:16:08.710 --> 00:16:11.550
he'd accomplished a magnificent feat.

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:14.890
That's what they say.

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:20.390
All in spite of the fact that there were villagers who opposed the proposal all the way to the end.

00:16:20.640 --> 00:16:21.560
I see!

00:16:21.560 --> 00:16:26.270
If we assume a grudge over the construction of the dam was the culprit's true motive...

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:31.070
Then our culprit may be one of the villagers or someone connected to it.

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:34.700
I was only stating one possibility, though.

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:40.870
It so happens that next Sunday...They're having a ceremony at the replacement village commemorating the fifth anniversary of thier relocation.

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:44.580
I heard the governor had been planning to attend and stay for a night.

00:16:45.130 --> 00:16:47.590
But, due to the bombing incident, it was canceled.

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:53.180
I get it! You want to visit that village and investigate the matter?

00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:56.180
Yeah. Professor, can you take me there?

00:16:56.180 --> 00:16:57.930
Where are you going?

00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:00.270
Bring us along too!

00:17:00.520 --> 00:17:02.390
It's always just Conan, how unfair!

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:05.270
Weren't you guys playing games?

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:07.810
If the professor's going, I'' tag along too.

00:17:08.190 --> 00:17:08.900
Haibara...

00:17:10.070 --> 00:17:13.450
Whenever I take my eyes off him, even for a moment, he starts hitting the pound key.

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:18.950
Nah... HaHaHa...

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:22.370
He's already been overweight for ages though.

00:17:33.090 --> 00:17:35.760
Kitanosawa Village

00:17:58.030 --> 00:17:59.620
It'll be our turn soon.

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:01.080
I'm really excited!

00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:15.720
So cold!

00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:17.590
But the snow is so soft!

00:18:17.720 --> 00:18:19.260
This is fantastic!

00:18:19.430 --> 00:18:21.430
All right, let's slide one more time.

00:18:21.470 --> 00:18:22.510
Yeah!

00:18:25.810 --> 00:18:27.980
They sure look happy, those kids.

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:29.610
Yeah. You're right.

00:18:29.690 --> 00:18:32.520
I'd say...It's a good thing we brought them.

00:18:33.610 --> 00:18:36.110
Well, regardless of those guys...

00:18:37.070 --> 00:18:38.610
Let's go, Ran!

00:18:38.780 --> 00:18:40.870
Wait... Sonoko!

00:18:41.660 --> 00:18:43.450
Geez, don't push me!

00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:44.700
Sorry, sorry.

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:47.960
Geez, why did ran and Sonoko come?

00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:48.960
Not to mention...

00:19:00.090 --> 00:19:03.810
There it is... The elusive open-air spa.

00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:08.560
What's more...It's a mixed bath!

00:19:10.150 --> 00:19:12.980
It's the mixed bath open-air spa of my dreams!

00:19:13.150 --> 00:19:18.860
Who await's me? A sexy lady? Maybe a beautiful virgin?

00:19:19.070 --> 00:19:19.820
All right!

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:29.290
Here Comes!

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:45.260
My... Nice water temperature, right?

00:19:48.480 --> 00:19:50.390
Being like this beneath an unfamiliar sky...

00:19:50.770 --> 00:19:56.230
Gazing upon the snowy view while immersing in a hot spring...Poetique, isn't it? Young miss.

00:20:07.660 --> 00:20:09.250
Which one should I eat?

00:20:09.370 --> 00:20:11.170
They all look delicious!

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:14.000
Uwah..Takoyaki is the best!

00:20:14.170 --> 00:20:15.670
Ikayaki is awesome, too!

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:17.300
Isobeyaki are delicious too, you know!

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:20.760
All right, I shall eat 'em all one by one!

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:25.100
Before that, here's a quiz!

00:20:25.140 --> 00:20:30.640
What's the most suitable menu for a food stand in a plaza covered in powder snow?

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:34.100
Number 1: Yakiimo

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:37.610
Number 2: Isobeyaki

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:41.150
Number 3: Ikayaki

00:20:41.650 --> 00:20:44.820
Number 4: Takoyaki

00:20:45.820 --> 00:20:47.830
What does powder snow mean?

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:49.580
It means light dry snow.

00:20:49.660 --> 00:20:50.870
Powder snow?

00:20:51.120 --> 00:20:57.040
Powder snow... Powder, powder... I know! It's number 4, takoyaki, right?

00:20:57.170 --> 00:20:58.880
Why?

00:20:59.460 --> 00:21:01.840
Because only takoyaki requires baking powder, right?

00:21:02.130 --> 00:21:04.470
Ayumi's mom always makes it!

00:21:04.590 --> 00:21:08.680
Beyond that, in Kansai, they nicknamed it "powder cuisine" according to Kazuha -chan.

00:21:08.850 --> 00:21:10.100
I see!

00:21:10.220 --> 00:21:14.690
But if that were the case, wouldn't it be too easy? It needs a twist.

00:21:14.810 --> 00:21:17.110
Excuse me, for not putting in a twist.

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:21.860
Well, I have a pop quiz of my own.

00:21:22.490 --> 00:21:25.700
Which of those is most suitable for the professor?

00:21:25.780 --> 00:21:26.370
Huh?

00:21:26.370 --> 00:21:29.660
The answer is none of them. They'll all make you even fatter.

00:21:31.410 --> 00:21:33.870
For starters, that wasn't even a quiz...

00:21:34.210 --> 00:21:35.870
Now then, we should...

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:37.130
Go eat some!

00:21:37.290 --> 00:21:39.590
I'll eat a bellyful, including the professor's share!

00:21:40.800 --> 00:21:42.170
We should go eat as well.

00:21:42.300 --> 00:21:44.840
Yeah! The professor's share, too!

00:21:46.180 --> 00:21:48.260
Ai-chan and Conan-kun, what will you do?

00:21:48.470 --> 00:21:49.600
I'll pass.

00:21:49.680 --> 00:21:52.980
Me too. I wanna take a walk through the village.

00:21:53.060 --> 00:21:55.560
Then, I'll go with Conan-kun and...

00:21:55.560 --> 00:21:58.440
You can't. Professor, you'll have a cup of tea with me.

00:22:02.820 --> 00:22:04.490
The map for Kitanosawa Village?

00:22:04.700 --> 00:22:08.070
Yeah. And also the guide for the dam, please.

00:22:08.120 --> 00:22:10.280
Understood. Hold on just a moment.

00:22:10.700 --> 00:22:15.210
Say, Yamao. I heard that ski site got shut down.

00:22:15.250 --> 00:22:19.540
Yeah. I heard about it too. They said avalanches have been hitting hard.

00:22:19.590 --> 00:22:20.590
Thank you for waiting.

00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:23.630
This is the map for Lake Kitanosawa.

00:22:23.840 --> 00:22:27.800
And this map is for the original Kitanosawa Village drawn to the same scale.

00:22:29.470 --> 00:22:31.640
Well...The guy really wanted to know

00:22:31.720 --> 00:22:36.270
where exactly in the dam reservoir his childhood home had sunk to.

00:22:36.440 --> 00:22:37.600
Dat so?

00:22:38.150 --> 00:22:39.770
Well, let's go.

00:22:43.530 --> 00:22:44.740
No good, no good.

00:22:45.820 --> 00:22:48.700
Say, mister, isn't that a stun gun?

00:22:49.660 --> 00:22:51.280
You know a lot, little kid.

00:22:51.830 --> 00:22:56.330
It's for my protection. When you're working as an insurance investigator in Tokyo...

00:22:56.750 --> 00:22:59.120
You constantly run into dangerous situations.

00:22:59.330 --> 00:23:02.040
That's why I always carry this whenever I go out.

00:23:02.380 --> 00:23:04.000
Well, see you later.

00:23:05.670 --> 00:23:06.720
Sorry for the wait.

00:23:07.340 --> 00:23:11.640
Let's see...A map for Kitanosawa Village and the guide to the dam, right?

00:23:11.800 --> 00:23:12.890
Here ya go.

00:23:13.100 --> 00:23:14.260
Thank you.

00:23:14.430 --> 00:23:18.560
Say...About the villagers who opposed the construction of the dam...

00:23:18.640 --> 00:23:19.350
Eh?

00:23:19.560 --> 00:23:21.310
Are they still living in the new village?

00:23:21.650 --> 00:23:23.820
Why ya asking somethin' like that?

00:23:23.820 --> 00:23:27.530
Ah! Just...For my winter vacation school project...

00:23:27.650 --> 00:23:29.200
What grade ya in?

00:23:29.320 --> 00:23:30.530
First grade...

00:23:30.740 --> 00:23:35.200
In that case, why don't ya choose a subject more suitable for your age?

00:23:35.290 --> 00:23:38.870
For example, look..Near this village, in the Lake Sawajiri,

00:23:39.040 --> 00:23:41.710
a lotta swans've come over to stay for now.

00:23:41.790 --> 00:23:44.290
Observin' the swans is a good idea!

00:23:44.340 --> 00:23:46.710
Since Lake Sawajiri's full's hot springs,

00:23:46.800 --> 00:23:49.170
it don't freeze even in the middle of winter!

00:23:49.470 --> 00:23:51.510
Is that so? I'll give it some thought!

00:23:52.180 --> 00:23:54.510
No suprise he's not gonna tell a kid, huh?

00:23:55.350 --> 00:23:57.640
Ah.. It hurts...

00:23:58.270 --> 00:24:00.020
All right, here's your medicine.

00:24:00.480 --> 00:24:02.310
Thank you very much...

00:24:02.520 --> 00:24:06.900
If you take it, you'll get better soon. And that overfilled stomach of yours will, too.

00:24:09.900 --> 00:24:13.870
Geez...All because you got carried away and ate ten plates of takoyaki!

00:24:14.030 --> 00:24:15.830
You're flattering me....

00:24:16.160 --> 00:24:17.080
It wasn't a praise.

00:24:17.160 --> 00:24:18.250
I'm sorry.

00:24:19.330 --> 00:24:20.870
What grades are you guys in?

00:24:20.870 --> 00:24:22.420
First grade!

00:24:22.790 --> 00:24:24.590
I see, first graders?

00:24:24.710 --> 00:24:25.420
Desu.

00:25:14.720 --> 00:25:16.180
That was delicious!

00:25:16.430 --> 00:25:17.760
So true!

00:25:17.850 --> 00:25:20.350
If they'd had eel rice, I would've had nothing to whine about!

00:25:20.430 --> 00:25:24.850
But your stomach sure can take a lot, even after eating so much for lunch.

00:25:24.940 --> 00:25:27.770
He has more than one stomach, that Genta-kun.

00:25:27.940 --> 00:25:29.530
I can still stuff more in it!

00:25:31.360 --> 00:25:35.660
That's right. Hey, let's buy a souvenir for Kobayashi-sensei!

00:25:36.450 --> 00:25:37.490
Great idea!

00:25:37.570 --> 00:25:39.370
They also have my eel pies on sale!

00:25:39.700 --> 00:25:41.200
Geez! He's planning to eat even more?

00:25:41.370 --> 00:25:42.450
Conan-kun, let's go take a look.

00:25:45.750 --> 00:25:48.250
I'll be heading for my room.

00:25:49.250 --> 00:25:53.260
"Snowshoe Trekking"...Lake Sawajiri?

00:25:54.420 --> 00:25:55.930
Hey, hey, miss!

00:25:56.180 --> 00:25:57.550
What is it, young boy?

00:25:57.720 --> 00:26:01.720
About this snowshoe trekking tour, does it go near the dam?

00:26:01.770 --> 00:26:05.940
Let's see... At a guest's request, we can tour nearby.

00:26:06.440 --> 00:26:08.230
Boy, are you interested in the dam?

00:26:08.360 --> 00:26:09.360
Could say that.

00:26:12.190 --> 00:26:13.650
What would be best?

00:26:14.280 --> 00:26:16.700
Must be these bear buns, hands down!

00:26:16.700 --> 00:26:20.830
No, owls are better! It gives off an intellectual vibe, too.

00:26:20.950 --> 00:26:24.410
Ai chan, what do you think is good?

00:26:26.040 --> 00:26:27.960
A coffee mug?

00:26:29.710 --> 00:26:31.630
I love swans?

00:26:32.750 --> 00:26:34.510
"I love Shiratori"

00:26:37.800 --> 00:26:40.220
What's wrong, Shiratori-kun? A cold?

00:26:40.260 --> 00:26:45.180
No. Until we apprehend our culprit...I can't be sitting around catching a cold.

00:26:51.060 --> 00:26:53.730
Can i even finish this before next winter?

00:26:54.230 --> 00:26:56.740
Say, Ran, what's your opinion on this?

00:26:57.570 --> 00:26:58.490
My opinion?

00:26:58.660 --> 00:27:00.820
It's a souvenir for Makoto-san!

00:27:00.870 --> 00:27:05.290
It's nice, isn't it? Really cute. Even looks a little like Sonoko.

00:27:05.370 --> 00:27:06.790
That so?

00:27:09.500 --> 00:27:10.540
Are you all set, Ran?

00:27:10.670 --> 00:27:12.750
All set on what?

00:27:13.090 --> 00:27:16.670
What else--on a souvenir for Shinichi-kun!

00:27:16.970 --> 00:27:18.260
It's fine, it's fine!

00:27:18.380 --> 00:27:22.050
I bet with all those investigations he wouldn't be available even if i did buy one.

00:27:23.350 --> 00:27:26.180
If you allow him to wander around without putting a collar on him...

00:27:26.430 --> 00:27:29.770
Maybe some random girl will show up and put one around his neck instead!

00:27:29.900 --> 00:27:33.070
A collar? She consider me a dog?

00:27:33.650 --> 00:27:38.280
Well...Regarding the "wandering around" part, I could say the same for Makoto-san.

00:27:38.740 --> 00:27:42.530
Well, maybe i should call him just in case?

00:27:44.030 --> 00:27:44.790
No good!

00:27:54.290 --> 00:27:55.420
Hello?

00:27:55.550 --> 00:27:58.920
Shinichi? Where do you think I am?

00:28:00.050 --> 00:28:04.930
I'm in Kitanosawa Village in Niigata Prefecture. We're all here for the Snow Festival...

00:28:05.060 --> 00:28:06.810
Wah...Amazing...

00:28:07.140 --> 00:28:07.930
What is it?

00:28:08.520 --> 00:28:10.890
The illuminations are so fabulous.

00:28:11.020 --> 00:28:14.110
And since it's snowing, everything looks so magical!

00:28:14.980 --> 00:28:17.320
I want you to see this too, Shinichi.

00:28:18.190 --> 00:28:23.070
If it's that impressive, I'd love to see it too.

00:28:25.580 --> 00:28:26.870
What kind of souvenir do you want?

00:28:27.410 --> 00:28:29.870
Anything is fine.

00:28:29.910 --> 00:28:34.130
I can't decide if you said anything is fine! Just name something.

00:28:34.290 --> 00:28:36.800
Geez... Well, what do they have there?

00:28:37.300 --> 00:28:40.880
Lots of things. For example, there are bear buns...

00:28:41.220 --> 00:28:45.800
Wooden owl sculptures... And mugs with swans on them.

00:28:45.890 --> 00:28:48.140
Swans...

00:28:49.140 --> 00:28:50.520
What the hell?

00:28:50.980 --> 00:28:53.060
Then, the owl.

00:28:53.100 --> 00:28:54.560
Got it--the owl, right?

00:28:54.650 --> 00:28:59.780
Well, I don't know when I'll be able to receive it, so...Just leave it in my living room or something.

00:28:59.860 --> 00:29:02.780
Geez...You need to come back once in a while!

00:29:03.070 --> 00:29:04.700
I know I should.

00:29:07.910 --> 00:29:10.290
Where are those guys going this late?

00:29:10.450 --> 00:29:11.660
Hey, Shinichi?

00:29:12.120 --> 00:29:15.880
Sorry, I'm kinda busy right now. Talk to you later.

00:29:17.630 --> 00:29:20.460
Ah! Shinichi! Geez...

00:29:23.970 --> 00:29:25.340
As a precaution...

00:29:28.060 --> 00:29:29.010
Oh, no!

00:29:38.860 --> 00:29:43.860
This is...A list of souvenirs I just mentioned...

00:29:44.950 --> 00:29:46.950
Then, the owl.

00:29:51.200 --> 00:29:54.540
Could it be...Shinichi...

00:30:02.010 --> 00:30:03.340
Awesome!

00:30:06.180 --> 00:30:07.640
So fast, so fast!

00:30:07.800 --> 00:30:09.810
I've been waiting to ride one of these for so long!

00:30:09.810 --> 00:30:11.680
Yeah, this is the best! Isn't it?

00:30:16.020 --> 00:30:18.980
Amazing, amazing! Just like a roller coaster!

00:30:18.980 --> 00:30:20.360
Totally thrilling!

00:30:20.400 --> 00:30:21.780
There's more to come!

00:30:25.200 --> 00:30:26.530
Hold on, Genta-kun!

00:30:26.660 --> 00:30:27.610
It's dangerous!

00:30:27.910 --> 00:30:30.580
Don't worry, don't worry! Just leave it to me!

00:30:30.990 --> 00:30:32.490
Genta-kun!

00:30:32.370 --> 00:30:33.040
Ahead, ahead!

00:30:32.950 --> 00:30:33.660
What?

00:30:51.100 --> 00:30:55.270
Hey, Genta-kun... Could we have gone off course?

00:30:55.350 --> 00:30:57.060
Eh..Think so?

00:30:57.350 --> 00:31:00.520
This is bad! I don't want to ride on a public road!

00:31:00.610 --> 00:31:03.570
Really? Then, let's go back!

00:31:13.540 --> 00:31:15.200
Hey, you alive?

00:31:15.750 --> 00:31:16.790
Barely...

00:31:17.250 --> 00:31:19.790
The snow acted like a cushion...

00:31:21.710 --> 00:31:23.340
This is bad, huh?

00:31:23.380 --> 00:31:26.300
It doesn't look like we can flip back over with only our strength.

00:31:26.670 --> 00:31:27.930
What do we do?

00:31:28.010 --> 00:31:33.140
I don't think the snow's gonna stop...And it's too far to walk our way back.

00:31:33.720 --> 00:31:36.640
On top of that, I don't think any cars are going to pass here!

00:31:37.390 --> 00:31:41.810
We'll be fine! We're carrying this, aren't we?

00:31:45.230 --> 00:31:48.400
Geez, those guys...Doing whatever they like!

00:31:48.650 --> 00:31:53.530
But isn't it a relief? That you have your upgraded skateboard to ride on snowy roads.

00:31:54.030 --> 00:31:55.580
Yeah, guess so.

00:31:57.250 --> 00:31:58.660
Over there, huh?

00:32:01.330 --> 00:32:03.960
He's so late , that Conan...

00:32:04.040 --> 00:32:07.170
But, the inside of a snow is quite warm, isn't it?

00:32:07.260 --> 00:32:11.050
Yeah. Hmm? Did you guys hear something?

00:32:14.140 --> 00:32:15.220
It's Conan-kun!

00:32:22.810 --> 00:32:24.060
You're too late, Conan!

00:32:24.190 --> 00:32:25.980
So Ai-chan came too!

00:32:26.150 --> 00:32:30.360
Since we're all unfamiliar with these snowy roads, I felt uneasy letting Edogawa-kun go alone.

00:32:31.570 --> 00:32:36.950
I see. Without calling an adult, there's nothing that can be done.

00:32:37.870 --> 00:32:41.040
We'll have to call the professor and have him pick us up right away.

00:32:41.080 --> 00:32:46.340
But I didn't want the professor and the others to know! That's why I had you help us in secret!

00:32:46.420 --> 00:32:48.710
What choice do we have? Besides...

00:32:48.300 --> 00:32:52.180
It's all Genta-kun's fault! You were in way over your head!

00:32:52.340 --> 00:32:54.640
Weren't you really excited about it too, Mitsuhiko?

00:32:54.640 --> 00:32:58.640
But there's a limit to everything! You need to think things through before you act!

00:32:58.720 --> 00:32:59.600
What'd you say!?

00:32:59.730 --> 00:33:01.310
Calm down, you two...

00:33:01.480 --> 00:33:03.850
You're talking like I wasn't thinking at all!

00:33:03.940 --> 00:33:06.730
Well? Did you think anything through at all?

00:33:07.020 --> 00:33:10.940
Of course I did! You're the one always pretending to look smart!

00:33:11.030 --> 00:33:13.700
What do you mean by that!? Genta-kun, you're a--!

00:33:13.740 --> 00:33:14.780
Mitsuhiko is a--!

00:33:14.570 --> 00:33:15.570
Knock it off!

00:33:16.330 --> 00:33:19.330
Both of you. Say nothing more than that.

00:33:19.830 --> 00:33:24.250
Once those words leave your mouth, you'll never be able to take them back.

00:33:24.420 --> 00:33:25.580
But--!

00:33:26.250 --> 00:33:27.710
Words are like swords.

00:33:28.250 --> 00:33:31.800
If you use them the wrong way, they'll turn into ugly weapons.

00:33:32.090 --> 00:33:36.010
There are cases of broken friendship that could have lasted a lifetime if not for verbal abuse.

00:33:39.470 --> 00:33:43.600
Once you sever your ties, you might not see each other ever again.

00:33:49.400 --> 00:33:51.360
A car's coming!

00:33:55.660 --> 00:34:00.620
Yeah. Well, we'll be back soon. Please tell others there's no need to worry about us.

00:34:00.790 --> 00:34:02.660
Got it. Stay safe then.

00:34:04.960 --> 00:34:08.130
You guys...Apologize when we get back.

00:34:08.540 --> 00:34:09.500
Understood...    Yes...

00:34:12.380 --> 00:34:14.800
My bad, Mitsuhiko.

00:34:15.170 --> 00:34:17.130
No, it was my fault.

00:34:22.390 --> 00:34:26.940
You guys are lucky! If i hadn't agree to meet someone at the louge,

00:34:27.100 --> 00:34:29.520
I wouldn't have been passing by at this hour.

00:34:29.690 --> 00:34:32.480
Mister, you don't live in Kitanosawa Village?

00:34:32.650 --> 00:34:38.490
I live by myself in a cottage I build in the mountains back there. Carving owls as a pastime.

00:34:38.660 --> 00:34:41.080
The wooden owl sculptures?

00:34:41.200 --> 00:34:42.620
Mister, you made those?

00:34:42.740 --> 00:34:48.460
I made the small ones at the cottage. And the big ones at the workshed near the dam.

00:34:48.630 --> 00:34:49.380
Dam?

00:34:49.710 --> 00:34:55.460
I once live in the village, but...It got sunk by that cursed dam, so that's why.

00:34:55.880 --> 00:35:00.510
Say...Could one of the people who opposed the construction of the dam to the end be...

00:35:00.640 --> 00:35:06.440
Yeah, I was. The villagers who originally opposed the plan, and my own parents...

00:35:06.770 --> 00:35:09.730
In the end, they all moved to the replacement village.

00:35:10.480 --> 00:35:12.320
That village is just rubbish to me!

00:35:15.400 --> 00:35:16.700
We're sorry...

00:35:17.320 --> 00:35:18.530
You brats--!

00:35:18.660 --> 00:35:22.490
Now, now, Mouri-kun. Those three regret their actions, after all.

00:35:22.580 --> 00:35:24.080
Yeah, but...

00:35:24.200 --> 00:35:25.410
Plus, look.

00:35:25.660 --> 00:35:28.920
Thank you very much! For going through the trouble to bring them back.

00:35:28.960 --> 00:35:32.630
Nah.  I happened to have things to attend to at this lodge.

00:35:32.750 --> 00:35:33.750
Is that so?

00:35:33.880 --> 00:35:35.340
Then, I'll get going.

00:35:35.510 --> 00:35:37.930
Yes. Thank you again.

00:35:38.180 --> 00:35:40.390
Hey, you guys need to thank him.

00:35:40.970 --> 00:35:42.800
Thank you very much!

00:35:43.310 --> 00:35:45.350
Don't make others worry again.

00:35:45.560 --> 00:35:46.680
Yes, sir!

00:35:46.980 --> 00:35:50.810
Now, how about we go back in? Bet you're all freezing, right?

00:35:50.900 --> 00:35:51.480
Yeah.

00:35:51.610 --> 00:35:53.480
I though I was gonna freeze to death.

00:35:53.570 --> 00:35:56.240
Who was it that made a fuss about wanting to ride a snowmobile?

00:35:56.280 --> 00:35:57.610
IT WAS GENTA-KUN!

00:36:00.200 --> 00:36:02.870
Hey, Mutou. Over here.

00:36:03.530 --> 00:36:04.580
You're late.

00:36:04.700 --> 00:36:06.910
Ah! It's the nurse from earlier!

00:36:07.040 --> 00:36:08.330
You're right!

00:36:08.710 --> 00:36:10.080
Thank you for earlier!

00:36:10.120 --> 00:36:12.710
Good evening. How's your stomach doing?

00:36:13.130 --> 00:36:14.550
It's all perfectly fine now!

00:36:14.630 --> 00:36:17.130
Genta-kun has a stomach made of iron!

00:36:14.920 --> 00:36:17.460
HUh? Those two...

00:36:19.170 --> 00:36:23.100
Excuse me, but could you be that famous detective Mouri Kogorou-san?

00:36:23.300 --> 00:36:29.940
You got it...I'm the great Detective Mouri Kogorou!

00:36:30.100 --> 00:36:30.940
Uh?

00:36:31.230 --> 00:36:32.270
As I thought!

00:36:32.520 --> 00:36:35.270
Then, are you here investigating some sort of case?

00:36:35.610 --> 00:36:36.860
NAh...

00:36:36.940 --> 00:36:39.700
We're here for the Snow Festival.

00:36:39.820 --> 00:36:42.160
Would we bring kids with us to work?

00:36:42.360 --> 00:36:44.280
Guess you're right.

00:36:44.370 --> 00:36:46.080
Haha..Of course!

00:36:47.660 --> 00:36:53.170
Well, to think we're able to meet with a great detective at a place like this! Right?

00:36:53.500 --> 00:36:58.090
Allow me to introduce ourselves. The guy sitting next to me is Yamao Keisuke.

00:36:59.420 --> 00:37:04.890
The ladies facing him are...Toono Mizuki and...Tachihara Fuyumi.

00:37:05.680 --> 00:37:07.850
And this is Mutou Takehiko.

00:37:09.470 --> 00:37:12.020
Finally, I'm Hikawa Shougo.

00:37:13.270 --> 00:37:16.400
Everyone here was born in the original Kitanosawa Village.

00:37:16.770 --> 00:37:21.990
Yamao and I got out from Tokyo and came all the way here in order to attend the ceremony.

00:37:22.360 --> 00:37:24.990
Then, you guys are childhood friends?

00:37:25.120 --> 00:37:27.740
Yes, we were elementary schoolmates.

00:37:28.080 --> 00:37:33.580
But, since it was a branch school in the village...The five of us were all that made up our class.

00:37:33.750 --> 00:37:35.420
Only five people?

00:37:35.500 --> 00:37:39.670
Yeah, that's right. It's been what, eight years since the five of us got together?

00:37:39.840 --> 00:37:41.170
Eight years?

00:37:41.420 --> 00:37:43.800
It's literally a touching class reunion!

00:37:43.930 --> 00:37:47.510
But, say...Why hadn't you met up in the past eight years?

00:37:48.560 --> 00:37:51.930
Well, about that...It's due to this.

00:37:55.980 --> 00:37:57.900
Wait--not now, Hikawa-kun!

00:37:58.110 --> 00:37:59.780
Isn't that...

00:38:00.360 --> 00:38:04.110
Eight years ago, this guy was still living in Tokyo...

00:38:04.150 --> 00:38:07.410
And while en route to his grandmother's place in the original village...

00:38:34.890 --> 00:38:40.230
This guy, scared, left her body alone like that, and escape by hiding himself in the village.

00:38:42.440 --> 00:38:47.450
Then, after a few hours, he change his mind and turned himself over to the police.

00:38:47.820 --> 00:38:49.410
He gave himself up?

00:38:50.370 --> 00:38:55.410
Yeah. My car was almost totaled...And I didn't think I could flee from it.

00:38:55.660 --> 00:39:01.590
At the same time, he owed a huge debt to loan sharks as a result of his gambling problem. His life was complete mess.

00:39:01.960 --> 00:39:06.090
In court, he was found guilty of speeding, DUI, hit-and-run...

00:39:06.550 --> 00:39:08.800
And of top of all that, his driver's license had already been suspended.

00:39:09.140 --> 00:39:13.680
After serving the time from all his punishment, it wasn't until this summer that he was set free.

00:39:13.770 --> 00:39:16.640
Then, while Yamao-san was still in prison...

00:39:16.940 --> 00:39:21.320
The proposal for the dam came in, and the whole village ended up being sunk into it.

00:39:21.770 --> 00:39:26.360
Yamao-kun's grandmother...Fell ill due to the shock of her grandson's incident...

00:39:26.820 --> 00:39:28.530
And drew here last breath.

00:39:29.030 --> 00:39:31.620
Then, she didn't get to live in the new village?

00:39:34.040 --> 00:39:35.540
Adding insult to injury,

00:39:35.870 --> 00:39:42.710
the victim killed in his accident was...The then 18-year old Mizuki's little sister, Natsuki!

00:39:49.430 --> 00:39:54.350
Yamao-kun...I still haven't forgiven you for what you did, even now.

00:39:56.140 --> 00:39:58.890
I too haven't forgiven a certain someone. Hikawa!

00:39:59.440 --> 00:40:01.560
When the proposal for the dam dropped in...

00:40:01.650 --> 00:40:04.940
You were the first to support it and sold the replacement land for a huge sum.

00:40:05.070 --> 00:40:08.450
You and your family then made off for Tokyo--I'll never forgive you lot!

00:40:08.450 --> 00:40:09.910
Hey, hey, Mutou...

00:40:09.990 --> 00:40:12.780
The one who coached your parents into something so dirty was you, wasn't it?

00:40:13.160 --> 00:40:17.660
You sold our long-cherished hometown land! Don't you realize that!?

00:40:17.790 --> 00:40:21.710
You can't live in this world without putting your wits to good use!

00:40:22.330 --> 00:40:25.710
Well, we've intruded enough. Let's head back to our rooms.

00:40:25.880 --> 00:40:29.340
Good idea. No good bothering these good folks any longer.

00:40:29.840 --> 00:40:31.550
Everyone, return to your rooms.

00:40:31.720 --> 00:40:32.640
Let's do that.

00:40:32.970 --> 00:40:34.680
Sorry to have bothered you all.

00:40:42.770 --> 00:40:47.940
That woman...The one named Fuyumi...She seems to have her own troubles too.

00:40:48.440 --> 00:40:49.490
Yeah.

00:40:51.610 --> 00:40:56.950
Even though they're elementary schoolmates...They've already gone separate ways in life.

00:40:57.240 --> 00:40:58.870
You're right.

00:41:01.960 --> 00:41:05.000
Don't worry, I'm certain that you guys will do well.

00:41:05.090 --> 00:41:07.210
Why?

00:41:07.840 --> 00:41:11.180
Of course I know! What you're thinking about right now.

00:41:11.550 --> 00:41:17.180
"I wonder what will happen between Shinichi and me?" Like that!

00:41:17.640 --> 00:41:23.190
Not that...I was just thinking about those people just now...And nothing about Him!

00:41:24.150 --> 00:41:27.400
Well, about the souvenir we were discussing earlier...

00:41:27.520 --> 00:41:30.190
Has Shinichi-kun really come to this village?

00:41:30.360 --> 00:41:34.620
Yeah. But it doen't seem he's staying at this lodge.

00:41:34.660 --> 00:41:40.250
Still...I have a feeling that Shinichi is somewhere really close to me.

00:41:40.620 --> 00:41:41.290
Eh?

00:41:42.410 --> 00:41:45.880
Then again, I always have that sort of feeling.

00:41:56.760 --> 00:42:01.430
You sold our long-cherished hometown land! Don't you realize that!?

00:42:01.770 --> 00:42:05.350
Is that Mutou-san related to the bombing incident in some way?

00:42:06.360 --> 00:42:09.780
And, those so-called classmates...

00:42:31.260 --> 00:42:32.260
So white!

00:42:31.920 --> 00:42:33.590
Snow, snow!

00:42:33.420 --> 00:42:34.680
Let's have a snowball fight!

00:42:34.630 --> 00:42:35.720
Let's do it!

00:42:40.260 --> 00:42:42.600
Conan-kun and Ai-chan, join us too!

00:42:42.980 --> 00:42:44.480
I'll pass.

00:42:44.810 --> 00:42:48.650
If we don't watch those guys, we'll never know what they're up to.

00:42:54.070 --> 00:42:55.030
We did it!

00:42:58.160 --> 00:43:01.490
All right, you guys! If you want a fight, you got one!

00:43:02.290 --> 00:43:04.040
Here he comes!

00:43:14.010 --> 00:43:15.050
Let's run!

00:43:16.220 --> 00:43:19.300
Here goes! Wait up, you guys!

00:43:20.050 --> 00:43:21.970
We're right here!

00:43:45.750 --> 00:43:47.290
There they are!

00:43:56.670 --> 00:43:58.630
Someone's watching us!

00:44:06.060 --> 00:44:08.690
Looks like he has something to say to us.

00:44:08.850 --> 00:44:10.310
Good morning!

00:44:21.660 --> 00:44:24.280
I...

00:44:25.950 --> 00:44:29.870
We're sorry...For stepping on your property.

00:44:34.000 --> 00:44:40.090
Can I...Join? Your group...

00:44:41.260 --> 00:44:49.520
Can I...Join You for a...Snow fight?

00:44:49.810 --> 00:44:52.230
That big bro looks a little weird, huh?

00:44:52.560 --> 00:44:54.770
Yeah...He seems childish or something...

00:45:00.570 --> 00:45:03.450
To...Touma...

00:45:09.250 --> 00:45:12.620
You finally woke up! Touma!

00:45:13.580 --> 00:45:15.920
Touma...Touma!

00:45:16.710 --> 00:45:19.460
Huh? Mommy?

00:45:21.220 --> 00:45:24.430
This is great! I finally get to see Mommy!

00:45:25.180 --> 00:45:26.350
Touma...

00:45:26.430 --> 00:45:27.100
This is great...

00:45:32.440 --> 00:45:36.520
Fuyumi's son, Touma...One morning eight years ago,

00:45:36.610 --> 00:45:40.150
he fell into a brook from a cliff near the original village.

00:45:40.240 --> 00:45:43.160
He was found in an unconscious state.

00:45:43.990 --> 00:45:49.790
Touma was immediately transported to the hospital at the foot of the mountain...And though his life was saved...

00:45:50.040 --> 00:45:53.620
He had never regained consciousness over the past eight years.

00:45:53.710 --> 00:45:54.460
Eight years?

00:45:54.710 --> 00:45:58.050
The day also coincides with Yamao's hit-and-run incident.

00:45:58.170 --> 00:46:00.340
The same day?

00:46:00.510 --> 00:46:07.510
Yeah. In a laid-back, literally peaceful village like ours...The fact that two major incidents occurred on the same day...

00:46:07.720 --> 00:46:09.430
It sent the whole village into chaos.

00:46:09.970 --> 00:46:12.230
What's the nature of Touma-kun's case?

00:46:12.310 --> 00:46:15.230
According to the police investigation, it was an accident.

00:46:15.650 --> 00:46:19.820
That cliff was close to Touma's favourite lake. where swans would gather.

00:46:20.280 --> 00:46:23.740
And since he had binoculars hanging around his neck when he was found...

00:46:24.280 --> 00:46:26.490
They deemed it an accidental slip and fall.

00:46:29.540 --> 00:46:33.750
The one who found Touma was the neighbour's dog--a dog he considered a dear friend.

00:46:34.250 --> 00:46:36.420
Where were Fuyumi-san and her husband then?

00:46:37.000 --> 00:46:39.290
She was an unmarried mother.

00:46:39.710 --> 00:46:44.300
Fuyumi was on call for an emergency patient at the hospital near the foot of the mountain she worked.

00:46:44.590 --> 00:46:47.090
So he doesn't have a grandfather or grandmother?

00:46:47.470 --> 00:46:51.350
Right. Fuyumi's parents got caught in an avalanche a while back.

00:46:52.430 --> 00:46:53.680
So they died?

00:46:54.810 --> 00:46:57.900
By the time they were found, 30 minutes had passed since the onset of the avalanche.

00:46:58.360 --> 00:47:01.900
We were told they could been saved if they had been found 15 minutes earlier.

00:47:02.280 --> 00:47:08.120
Once you're caught in an avalanche, it's said you have a time limit of 15 minutes.

00:47:08.620 --> 00:47:09.950
15 minutes?

00:47:10.330 --> 00:47:13.620
That quarter-hour determines life or death.

00:47:14.000 --> 00:47:15.580
It's too short if it's only a quarter.

00:47:18.290 --> 00:47:24.550
Well, it's all right for you to take a break from the clinic...So please keep Touma-kun company.

00:47:24.920 --> 00:47:28.680
Yeah. Thank you very much.

00:47:35.520 --> 00:47:36.810
How was it, Fuyumi?

00:47:37.480 --> 00:47:43.440
Mizuki...Mutou-kun...He said Touma was physically fine.

00:47:43.980 --> 00:47:44.820
That so...

00:47:45.440 --> 00:47:47.400
But...His mind...

00:47:49.030 --> 00:47:51.830
He has no memory of the day he fell from the cliff.

00:47:51.830 --> 00:47:52.450
Huh?

00:47:52.910 --> 00:47:59.370
So thing like, "Why did I sleep for the last eight years?" are incomprehensible to him.

00:48:01.340 --> 00:48:05.170
But this is great, Fuyumi. This is truly a miracle.

00:48:08.220 --> 00:48:11.640
Sorry for saying this...But would you consider switching to contact lenses?

00:48:14.720 --> 00:48:19.850
A beauty like yourself is suited for contacts much more so than glasses!

00:48:21.560 --> 00:48:24.270
I cannot help but view glasses as cold...

00:48:25.690 --> 00:48:27.530
And do not like them.

00:48:29.740 --> 00:48:31.200
Hold it, Dad!

00:48:35.740 --> 00:48:36.290
Geez...

00:48:41.630 --> 00:48:43.210
You looked intrigued.

00:48:44.340 --> 00:48:48.260
About Touma-kun's incident coinciding with Yamao-san's traffic accident from the same day.

00:48:48.760 --> 00:48:54.970
Yeah. Was it just a coincidence... Or...

00:48:56.060 --> 00:49:00.350
Auntie! Is it true Touma-kun regained consciousness?

00:49:00.850 --> 00:49:03.980
So you all came! Please come in.

00:49:04.520 --> 00:49:05.980
Will he be all right?

00:49:07.280 --> 00:49:09.490
Isn't it too early for him to see them?

00:49:10.530 --> 00:49:11.320
You're right.

00:49:16.700 --> 00:49:19.330
Touma, look, it's Kaori-chan and the others.

00:49:19.870 --> 00:49:21.370
Hey, doing all right?

00:49:21.920 --> 00:49:23.790
It's been a while, Touma-kun!

00:49:40.560 --> 00:49:41.980
Let's take a rest now.

00:49:42.440 --> 00:49:43.270
Yes!

00:49:44.150 --> 00:49:45.770
So many swans here!

00:50:01.540 --> 00:50:03.250
Huh...Mizuki-san!

00:50:03.960 --> 00:50:09.340
Yeah...I decided to try contact lenses. I did have some ready.

00:50:09.710 --> 00:50:14.470
My, they suit you better! Your beauty just rose to another level.

00:50:15.890 --> 00:50:17.350
Geez, shame on you, Dad!

00:50:18.010 --> 00:50:21.520
Hey, didn't she change her hairstyle a bit too?

00:50:22.640 --> 00:50:25.150
Maybe she really has a thing for Uncle!

00:50:25.400 --> 00:50:26.860
Knock it off, Sonoko!

00:50:28.320 --> 00:50:31.030
Wow, in all seriousness, you are beautiful!

00:50:32.150 --> 00:50:34.700
Say, say...

00:50:35.410 --> 00:50:37.660
The lake was right around here, right?

00:50:38.280 --> 00:50:39.080
That's right.

00:50:39.330 --> 00:50:41.660
Where was the cliff where Touma-san fell?

00:50:42.830 --> 00:50:43.580
Touma-kun?

00:50:44.290 --> 00:50:46.670
Right here.

00:50:47.140 --> 00:50:48.690
That's weird.

00:50:50.020 --> 00:50:53.320
If he was coming from this way, then the direction would be a bit off.

00:50:53.770 --> 00:50:57.490
He was lost, wasn't he? That's enough, you!

00:50:57.490 --> 00:51:01.240
Then, the place where Yamao-san had the accident was on this curve, right?

00:51:01.450 --> 00:51:05.330
That's true, but...Why do you ask?

00:51:05.990 --> 00:51:07.870
Take a hike over there.

00:51:09.000 --> 00:51:09.920
Conan-kun!

00:51:11.790 --> 00:51:12.920
It's snowing...

00:51:13.590 --> 00:51:14.630
It really is!

00:51:14.880 --> 00:51:16.050
Geez...

00:51:17.420 --> 00:51:19.170
Did you find something out again?

00:51:19.300 --> 00:51:24.640
Sort of. Whether Touma-kun really came to see the swans or not.

00:51:25.510 --> 00:51:26.680
Pretty!

00:51:27.020 --> 00:51:28.310
Looks like it's going to accumulate.

00:51:28.640 --> 00:51:29.600
It's all right!

00:51:31.400 --> 00:51:32.650
It'll stop soon.

00:51:33.360 --> 00:51:35.650
Well, we should get going now.

00:51:42.320 --> 00:51:43.620
It really stopped snowing!

00:51:44.120 --> 00:51:46.660
As expected, locals know best.

00:51:47.370 --> 00:51:52.500
Mizuki-san, would you consider visiting Tokyo next time? I can show you around!

00:51:53.130 --> 00:51:54.420
Then, how about the Sky Tree?

00:51:54.840 --> 00:51:57.550
Anywhere but that place...

00:51:59.010 --> 00:52:00.880
Are you afraid of heights, Mouri-san?

00:52:01.470 --> 00:52:04.680
This is embarassing...Anything you're afraid of, Mizuki-san?

00:52:05.010 --> 00:52:07.430
I can't stand dark, narrow places...

00:52:08.060 --> 00:52:09.350
Why'd you butt in like that?

00:52:09.470 --> 00:52:10.680
So what, I felt like it!

00:52:15.860 --> 00:52:17.360
What's wrong, Mizuki-san?

00:52:17.690 --> 00:52:20.900
say...That jacket, isn't it Hikawa-kun's?

00:52:21.700 --> 00:52:24.240
Hey, Hikawa-kun!

00:52:26.030 --> 00:52:27.030
He can't hear us?

00:52:27.580 --> 00:52:29.120
What's he doing out in a place like that?

00:52:29.790 --> 00:52:31.500
Hey..isn't that weird?

00:52:31.960 --> 00:52:32.290
Yeah.

00:52:32.710 --> 00:52:34.630
Everyone, please wait here for a bit.

00:52:36.340 --> 00:52:39.550
Hikawa-kun! What are you doing in a place like that?

00:52:40.590 --> 00:52:41.470
Dad...

00:52:41.880 --> 00:52:43.760
Yeah. I'll go check it out.

00:52:45.220 --> 00:52:46.720
Hikawa-kun, what's the matter?

00:52:49.890 --> 00:52:50.770
Hikawa-kun!

00:52:51.930 --> 00:52:53.810
Mizuki-san! What's wrong?

00:52:54.230 --> 00:52:55.850
Hikawa-kun doesn't look right!

00:52:56.810 --> 00:52:57.480
back off!

00:52:57.650 --> 00:52:58.150
Yes...

00:52:58.690 --> 00:53:00.570
Hikawa-san... Is something wrong?

00:53:00.980 --> 00:53:02.400
Hikawa-san... Hikawa-sa...

00:53:10.290 --> 00:53:11.080
Dad!

00:53:11.120 --> 00:53:12.790
Don't come! Stay back!

00:53:20.130 --> 00:53:22.460
It's no good. He's dead.

00:53:24.550 --> 00:53:25.380
Are you all right?

00:53:27.720 --> 00:53:29.720
Looks like there are no external wounds.

00:53:30.350 --> 00:53:33.270
Froze to death? No... Cardiac arrest?

00:53:34.810 --> 00:53:38.060
That reminds me, Hikawa-kun has had a heart problem since he was a child...

00:53:38.560 --> 00:53:42.030
So that was the case? Ran contact the police!

00:53:42.070 --> 00:53:43.740
Got it!

00:53:44.440 --> 00:53:45.700
Hey, this is strange.

00:53:47.410 --> 00:53:49.320
His stun gun is missing.

00:53:49.490 --> 00:53:51.700
Hey! Go somewhere else, brat!

00:53:51.870 --> 00:53:56.210
Hikawa-san said he always keeps a stun gun in his pocket as self-defense!

00:53:56.290 --> 00:53:56.960
Hmm?

00:53:57.080 --> 00:54:00.840
The fact that it's was missing means someone else was with him and took it away!

00:54:02.380 --> 00:54:04.340
No, that's not it.

00:54:05.470 --> 00:54:06.430
How come?

00:54:06.720 --> 00:54:07.630
Look at that.

00:54:10.850 --> 00:54:15.850
There's only one set of shoeprints. And there's no doubt they're from those snowshoes.

00:54:19.770 --> 00:54:24.070
In other words, Hikawa-san...walked here aloneside the brook from the village...

00:54:24.650 --> 00:54:30.570
And while walking on the snowfield, underwent cardiac arrest and died as a result. That must be it.

00:54:30.820 --> 00:54:32.280
Then, what about the stun gun?

00:54:32.830 --> 00:54:34.950
He must've left it back at the lodge!

00:54:35.330 --> 00:54:36.790
That can't be the case.

00:54:38.120 --> 00:54:40.630
But, those shoeprints...

00:54:40.790 --> 00:54:43.630
Could that have been a trick used by the culprit?

00:54:43.800 --> 00:54:44.340
Heh?

00:54:44.550 --> 00:54:45.050
What?

00:54:45.130 --> 00:54:50.260
Well, don't you hear it often? Mysteries about shoeprints left atop the snow!

00:54:50.430 --> 00:54:52.010
Look, you...

00:54:52.850 --> 00:54:58.480
Shoeprints...Atop the snow? I got it!

00:54:59.310 --> 00:55:01.730
This was indeed the culprit's trick!

00:55:03.070 --> 00:55:07.950
All right? Near the brook, the culprit already drugged Hikawa-san with poison or something...

00:55:08.150 --> 00:55:10.410
In order to kill him and disguise it as a heart attack.

00:55:11.030 --> 00:55:15.160
They then changed into a prearranged pair of boots like those Hikawa-san had been wearing...

00:55:15.620 --> 00:55:17.750
And carried his body on their back here.

00:55:18.330 --> 00:55:23.630
Then, they set hikawa-san down...And stole his stun gun.

00:55:24.420 --> 00:55:28.800
On their way back, they followed their own shoeprints...And walked backwards by stepping on them!

00:55:29.260 --> 00:55:30.590
Backwards?

00:55:30.800 --> 00:55:32.010
Is something like that possible?

00:55:32.590 --> 00:55:34.550
Of course it is!

00:55:41.190 --> 00:55:41.810
Just you watch!

00:55:54.370 --> 00:55:56.910
Why is there so much snow inside his hood?

00:55:58.330 --> 00:55:59.160
I see...

00:56:00.710 --> 00:56:04.540
I got it, Uncle! The culprit super easy trick!

00:56:04.790 --> 00:56:05.460
What?

00:56:05.920 --> 00:56:08.130
See, it was snowing earlier, wasn't it?

00:56:08.800 --> 00:56:12.090
The culprit walked alongside the brook with hikawa-san to here...

00:56:12.180 --> 00:56:14.890
And killed him off while disguising it as a heart attack.

00:56:15.550 --> 00:56:19.180
Then the snow that was coming down wiped away both of their shoeprints!

00:56:19.930 --> 00:56:22.980
And, after waiting until the snow stopped...

00:56:22.980 --> 00:56:26.980
The culprit changed into a prearranged pair of boots similar to Hikawa-san's...

00:56:27.690 --> 00:56:32.740
And walked backwards without concern for the length of their stride as they returned to the brook!

00:56:34.490 --> 00:56:39.240
See? If we do this, there will be only one set of shoeprints left, right?

00:56:40.120 --> 00:56:43.830
As for proof, look over there. The inside of Hikawa-san's coat hood.

00:56:44.170 --> 00:56:45.460
Lots of snow build up, right?

00:56:45.960 --> 00:56:51.920
I bet the culprit, after the snow had stopped...wiped off only the snow on his head and shoulders.

00:56:52.840 --> 00:56:56.350
All in order to make it seem they had come here after the snowfall!

00:56:56.760 --> 00:57:02.980
But, this trick...It wouldn't work if we hadn't quickly arrived here and found his body, right?

00:57:03.270 --> 00:57:06.060
If his body were left unfound, and should the snow fall again...

00:57:06.100 --> 00:57:08.520
The shoeprints they had left would've been erased again.

00:57:08.820 --> 00:57:14.820
Which means the perp is someone who was sure of our coming to this place beforehand, huh?

00:57:15.910 --> 00:57:19.280
Or maybe, it was the one who guided us here...

00:57:20.870 --> 00:57:23.960
About our coming here around this time...

00:57:24.160 --> 00:57:28.340
I think they could have estimated the time by using the snowshoe trekking information packet.

00:57:30.550 --> 00:57:32.380
She has a point.

00:57:33.130 --> 00:57:34.840
Say, say, Mizuki-san...

00:57:35.090 --> 00:57:38.300
Where do those shoeprints lead?

00:57:38.470 --> 00:57:40.680
Mutou-kun's mountain cottage is that way.

00:57:40.640 --> 00:57:41.930
Mutou-san's?

00:57:42.470 --> 00:57:47.690
But...There's a village road for cars that goes from the village to the mountains cottage.

00:57:47.690 --> 00:57:51.780
Was it the road we were riding on the snowmobile last night?

00:57:52.610 --> 00:57:56.820
Why did't Hikaru-kun take that road?

00:57:57.450 --> 00:58:01.790
No. Hikawan-san and the culprit purposely avoided that road...

00:58:02.700 --> 00:58:06.290
Instead walking from the brook to the mountain cottage via the snowfield, where they wouldn't be seen.

00:58:07.920 --> 00:58:08.710
Why is that?

00:58:14.210 --> 00:58:15.380
Thank you for your patience.

00:58:16.010 --> 00:58:22.390
Hikawa-san's body is now at a university hospital...And is being throughly investigated by the medical examiner.

00:58:22.850 --> 00:58:25.890
Preliminary results confirmed the cause of death was cardiac arrest, but...

00:58:26.230 --> 00:58:29.900
Whether it was due to natural causes or human-induced...

00:58:30.060 --> 00:58:32.770
Cannot be determined without a thorough investigation and autopsy.

00:58:33.320 --> 00:58:37.450
Human-induced? Are you saying someone murdered Hikawa?

00:58:37.860 --> 00:58:40.280
We cannot say at this point.

00:58:41.160 --> 00:58:45.750
Yamao-san, at around 2:00 PM, what were your actions and whereabouts?

00:58:47.580 --> 00:58:53.210
This afternoon, Hikawa and I went our sepera ways, and I took a stroll in the east side woods.

00:58:54.000 --> 00:58:55.260
All alone?

00:58:55.460 --> 00:58:56.090
Yeah.

00:58:56.420 --> 00:58:57.970
Did you bump into anyone?

00:58:58.300 --> 00:58:58.930
No.

00:58:59.340 --> 00:59:00.550
Understood.

00:59:01.470 --> 00:59:06.480
Next...Tachihara-san?

00:59:06.810 --> 00:59:11.860
I was with Touma, who was sleeping due to the fatigue from his morning checkup.

00:59:11.900 --> 00:59:13.440
So I was at my house.

00:59:14.110 --> 00:59:15.730
Can anyone verify that?

00:59:17.820 --> 00:59:18.530
I'm afraid not.

00:59:20.360 --> 00:59:21.660
Mutou-san?

00:59:22.240 --> 00:59:26.540
I'd returned to my workshed near the dam and kept working.

00:59:26.910 --> 00:59:28.290
Workshed??

00:59:28.910 --> 00:59:33.250
Not the mountain cottage near where Hikawa-san's body was found?

00:59:33.420 --> 00:59:34.000
Right.

00:59:34.630 --> 00:59:35.800
Is there anyone who can verify?

00:59:36.800 --> 00:59:40.680
No one! I don't meet up with people while I'm working!

00:59:40.970 --> 00:59:47.850
But, why was Hikawa-san walking toward your mountain cottage if that's so?

00:59:48.270 --> 00:59:49.890
How would i know about something like that?

00:59:50.230 --> 00:59:52.690
Were you really not at the mountain cottage?

00:59:53.400 --> 00:59:53.860
What?

00:59:54.520 --> 00:59:57.480
You called Hikawa out and killed him, didn't you?

00:59:57.650 --> 01:00:00.200
By telling him you wanted to talk about Mizuki or something!

01:00:00.570 --> 01:00:02.820
What do you mean by that?

01:00:03.700 --> 01:00:08.250
When Hikawa was younger, he once proposed to Mizuki but was rejected.

01:00:10.370 --> 01:00:13.170
But Hikawa still had lingering feeling for Mizuki even now.

01:00:13.790 --> 01:00:16.840
So if her name were to get mentioned, he would definitely go there.

01:00:19.090 --> 01:00:24.140
So that's how it was. I thought it was definitely Mutou-san who had the crush.

01:00:24.970 --> 01:00:27.970
How could you say that I was definitely the one who killed Hikawa!?

01:00:28.390 --> 01:00:31.440
Because it seems you guys were fighting about the dam!

01:00:31.980 --> 01:00:34.150
I'm too flabbergasted to reply to bullshit like that.

01:00:34.560 --> 01:00:37.150
Well then...Lastly, Toono-san?

01:00:39.570 --> 01:00:43.860
She was with us the entire time, so her alibi is solid.

01:00:44.240 --> 01:00:45.280
Is that so?

01:00:46.330 --> 01:00:50.080
I understand. That will be all for today.

01:00:50.700 --> 01:00:55.290
Once we confirm that Hikawa-san's death was a homicide...

01:00:55.460 --> 01:00:59.340
We will conduct another round of detailed questioning.

01:00:59.760 --> 01:01:02.300
Uhm, should we check their belongings?

01:01:02.590 --> 01:01:05.760
At this stage, we can't force them to comply, can we?

01:01:06.510 --> 01:01:11.560
Moreover, even if someone did steal the item, they would have hidden it somewhere by now.

01:01:12.270 --> 01:01:14.730
Eveyrone, thank you for your cooperation.

01:01:16.480 --> 01:01:18.520
That mister speaks really slowly, doesn't he?

01:01:18.770 --> 01:01:21.030
I thought I was gonna fall asleep...

01:01:30.540 --> 01:01:36.120
So cold! Why must we endure this in order to watch the sunrise?

01:01:36.420 --> 01:01:38.380
Stick with it, stick with it.

01:01:40.170 --> 01:01:43.590
I wonder who it was? The culprit who killed Hikawa-san.

01:01:44.260 --> 01:01:46.510
yeah... If it's Mutou-san...

01:01:47.510 --> 01:01:50.310
Based on the shoe prints... I think instead of the mountain cottage,

01:01:50.390 --> 01:01:52.180
he was waiting in the middle of the snowfields.

01:01:53.390 --> 01:01:56.230
And after the murder, he backtracked to the brook.

01:01:56.810 --> 01:01:57.310
Just...

01:01:57.480 --> 01:02:02.610
I don't understand why Hikawa-san had to walk past the brook and through the snowfield where no one could see him.

01:02:03.320 --> 01:02:06.700
Even is Mutou-san ordered him to do so, don't you think it's unnatural?

01:02:06.780 --> 01:02:07.410
You're right.

01:02:08.030 --> 01:02:10.330
I would've gone by car via the village road.

01:02:10.740 --> 01:02:15.540
Moreover, is there a connection between Hikawa-san's murder and the bombing accident?

01:02:16.670 --> 01:02:19.330
Even is there is, I don't think this is the end of it.

01:02:19.790 --> 01:02:21.880
Something else will definitely happen.

01:02:26.220 --> 01:02:27.300
Not again...

01:02:29.090 --> 01:02:31.100
(I can't come to the phone right now. Sorry for any inconvenience...)

01:02:31.310 --> 01:02:33.020
Not again.

01:02:33.140 --> 01:02:35.060
You got Shinichi-kun's auto message again?

01:02:35.350 --> 01:02:39.230
I wanted to talk to him about Hikawa-san, but...

01:02:39.480 --> 01:02:43.230
Could he really be here in this village? That deduction geek.

01:02:43.360 --> 01:02:45.150
That's what she said.

01:02:45.570 --> 01:02:46.530
Leave me alone.

01:02:46.650 --> 01:02:49.070
And, please, what time does she think it is?

01:02:51.660 --> 01:02:53.370
Hey, isn't that Touma-san?

01:02:59.790 --> 01:03:00.630
Kuro...

01:03:01.790 --> 01:03:02.630
Touma-kun!

01:03:02.710 --> 01:03:03.300
Touma!

01:03:03.380 --> 01:03:04.340
What's the matter, Touma-kun?

01:03:06.670 --> 01:03:08.300
"Kuro's Grave"...

01:03:08.970 --> 01:03:11.970
Kuro is the dog who found Touma-kun 8 years ago?

01:03:12.100 --> 01:03:15.770
Why...Is Kuro really dead?

01:03:16.180 --> 01:03:16.890
Touma!

01:03:17.810 --> 01:03:19.650
What are you doing out here!?

01:03:20.270 --> 01:03:21.100
Mom...

01:03:22.020 --> 01:03:24.320
Why did you come out without telling me!?

01:03:24.400 --> 01:03:25.860
Now, now ma'am...

01:03:26.070 --> 01:03:29.740
Why!? Why did I become like this!?

01:03:30.450 --> 01:03:31.820
I don't get it...

01:03:32.160 --> 01:03:35.790
All my friends become strangers...And Kuro is dead...

01:03:36.410 --> 01:03:39.040
I don't know what I'm supposed to do!

01:03:41.290 --> 01:03:42.630
I don't get it!

01:03:44.210 --> 01:03:46.170
Kuro...Kuro...

01:03:46.460 --> 01:03:47.130
Touma…

01:03:47.920 --> 01:03:51.300
You can't blame the kid. His body is that of a 15 year-old,

01:03:51.550 --> 01:03:54.010
but at heart he is still only 7.

01:03:54.810 --> 01:03:57.390
It's probably hard for him to keep a grasp on reality.

01:03:57.890 --> 01:03:59.890
That's just the opposite of us, isn't it?

01:04:00.520 --> 01:04:01.350
Touma...

01:04:01.770 --> 01:04:02.650
Mom!

01:04:14.870 --> 01:04:17.540
Look! The snow is glittering!

01:04:18.120 --> 01:04:20.710
This isn't snow, but...

01:04:21.160 --> 01:04:22.420
Diamond dust.

01:04:22.710 --> 01:04:26.000
Diamond!? There are gems coming down!?

01:04:26.380 --> 01:04:27.300
That's not it.

01:04:27.550 --> 01:04:32.510
The water vapor in the atmosphere solidifies due to the cold...

01:04:34.180 --> 01:04:36.600
Here. Touma-kun, look!

01:04:37.600 --> 01:04:38.850
It's really pretty!

01:04:52.860 --> 01:04:54.700
Awesome, right? It's a treasure!

01:05:04.710 --> 01:05:05.330
Touma?

01:05:08.460 --> 01:05:10.760
What happen? Are you all right, Touma?

01:05:11.630 --> 01:05:12.420
His memories...

01:05:13.430 --> 01:05:16.180
What was that? I saw the same lights before...

01:05:18.560 --> 01:05:20.350
No good, I can't remember!

01:05:20.810 --> 01:05:21.430
Touma!

01:05:21.520 --> 01:05:22.270
Touma-kun!

01:05:22.390 --> 01:05:23.020
Touma-san...

01:05:23.230 --> 01:05:23.850
Touma...

01:05:26.150 --> 01:05:28.570
I can't...Remember...

01:05:37.870 --> 01:05:40.450
The diamond dust was really pretty, wasn't it?

01:05:40.450 --> 01:05:42.960
Definitely! I felt I was in a fairyland!

01:05:43.790 --> 01:05:45.920
Hostess! One more bowl!

01:05:46.330 --> 01:05:49.090
Hey, the thing he was trying to remember...

01:05:49.250 --> 01:05:53.630
Yeah. It was likely part of his memories from when he fell from the cliff 8 years ago.

01:05:54.720 --> 01:05:55.840
I tried to investigate it, but...

01:05:56.550 --> 01:06:00.680
Because it had been snowing from dawn that day, there hadn't been an occurrence of diamond dust.

01:06:01.520 --> 01:06:04.810
In that case... What exactly was it that he saw?

01:06:07.440 --> 01:06:08.900
Oh, yeah, where are Genta and the rest?

01:06:09.360 --> 01:06:11.860
They said they were going to play with Touma-kun and went out.

01:06:11.990 --> 01:06:16.200
Geez...They'd better not be up to no good or something again!

01:06:18.320 --> 01:06:23.750
Hey, where are we going? If we go too far, I'll be scolded by my mom.

01:06:24.040 --> 01:06:25.000
Hey, Touma-kun!

01:06:25.620 --> 01:06:28.750
Shall we go near where you fell from the cliff?

01:06:29.040 --> 01:06:31.920
If we do that, you might start remembering lots of things!

01:06:32.340 --> 01:06:33.050
But...

01:06:33.380 --> 01:06:35.010
We'll be with you!

01:06:35.260 --> 01:06:36.470
uhm...

01:06:36.630 --> 01:06:37.430
Well?

01:06:38.470 --> 01:06:40.050
Gather your courage and go for it!

01:06:40.300 --> 01:06:41.970
Let's go!

01:06:42.430 --> 01:06:43.600
Yay! Let's do this!

01:06:58.160 --> 01:07:01.620
Now... Where did those kids go?

01:07:01.990 --> 01:07:05.700
Probably to the campsite? They're having the commemorative ceremony there.

01:07:06.120 --> 01:07:09.920
Yeah, it's said to start at 10:00 AM.

01:07:10.420 --> 01:07:12.880
Still a little over an hour.

01:07:13.130 --> 01:07:15.800
It'll be fine as long as they aren't up to any mischief. If they are, I'll definitely use my fist this time!

01:07:16.010 --> 01:07:17.720
It's the people from the dam.

01:07:18.760 --> 01:07:21.680
They probably came down to participate in the commemorative ceremony.

01:07:21.970 --> 01:07:25.270
That aside, is it really all right to leave the dam alone like that?

01:07:25.520 --> 01:07:26.600
No worries,

01:07:26.770 --> 01:07:28.810
there are two caretakers back there.

01:07:29.020 --> 01:07:30.940
You overheard me?

01:07:31.440 --> 01:07:34.070
At least let us have some coffee here.

01:07:34.360 --> 01:07:35.570
Thanks for the concern.

01:07:36.280 --> 01:07:37.150
Geez, Sonoko.

01:07:38.450 --> 01:07:40.660
I'll join you later, go ahead without me!

01:07:41.070 --> 01:07:42.450
You'll fall if you run!

01:07:42.660 --> 01:07:43.450
Got it!

01:07:45.450 --> 01:07:46.370
Hello!

01:07:47.700 --> 01:07:52.290
Miss, you're one of Touma-san's classmates right? Did you come to see Touma-san?

01:07:52.710 --> 01:07:56.380
Yeah, there was something I wanted to show him, but he seems to be out.

01:07:56.710 --> 01:07:58.760
What's this thing that you wanted to show him?

01:08:01.720 --> 01:08:05.010
So this is a photograph from 8 years ago, huh?

01:08:05.720 --> 01:08:07.720
We were about the same age as you.

01:08:08.310 --> 01:08:11.940
Huh, those binoculars...This was a school, right?

01:08:12.230 --> 01:08:12.980
Yes.

01:08:13.520 --> 01:08:15.360
He wore them around his neck even at school?

01:08:15.650 --> 01:08:20.200
Right. They were Touma-kun's trademark, so he'd always wear them whenever he went out.

01:08:20.570 --> 01:08:24.620
If that so, he wasn't necessarily out looking for swans.

01:08:25.870 --> 01:08:29.040
That was something Touma-kun gave me.

01:08:29.620 --> 01:08:32.160
He really loved Kuro, didn't he?

01:08:32.580 --> 01:08:36.840
I thought I'd show him the drawing and photograph while having a chat, but...

01:08:38.090 --> 01:08:39.880
Tha might hurt him more, I guess?

01:08:44.390 --> 01:08:50.310
Back then...Hikawa-san opened up the printed article that was folded twice from the outside and showed it to everyone.

01:08:51.230 --> 01:08:54.060
But, doesn't one usually fold the printed side inwards-

01:08:54.440 --> 01:08:56.730
to prevent it from getting dirty?

01:08:57.150 --> 01:08:58.360
Something wrong with the drawing?

01:08:58.980 --> 01:09:03.160
Nothing at all. Thanks for showing it to me.

01:09:04.870 --> 01:09:06.530
I gotta get back to the lodge!

01:09:07.160 --> 01:09:08.530
You'll fall if you run!

01:09:08.780 --> 01:09:09.740
I'll be all right!

01:09:13.410 --> 01:09:15.750
Hey, can I change the sheets inside?

01:09:16.750 --> 01:09:18.920
Hold on, ya opened the door?

01:09:19.210 --> 01:09:20.130
Huh? I wasn't supposed to?

01:09:21.010 --> 01:09:26.300
Of course yer not supposed to! They're gonna come and search for fingerprints and shoeprints.

01:09:26.640 --> 01:09:31.270
No way! What should I do? They're gonna suspect me!

01:09:31.560 --> 01:09:33.190
Right, they're gonna catch ya!

01:09:34.560 --> 01:09:35.730
Don't scare me like that!

01:09:48.530 --> 01:09:49.410
This is it.

01:09:52.120 --> 01:09:54.330
Jewelry shop robbery...

01:09:55.540 --> 01:09:57.330
"On the 15th at around 11:00 PM...

01:09:57.790 --> 01:10:01.090
"An unknown perpetrator broke into Misuzu Jewelry located in Yaoi City, Shinjuku Ward, Tokyo...

01:10:01.250 --> 01:10:06.800
"And stabbed 51-year-old company president Musuzu Eiko to death with a sharp blade.

01:10:07.510 --> 01:10:10.890
"The robbery allegedly made off with one billion yen worth of jewelry."

01:10:12.140 --> 01:10:16.690
This incident...If I recall, it happened when I was still in third grade...

01:10:17.150 --> 01:10:19.110
They still haven't found the culprit.

01:10:19.940 --> 01:10:22.730
But, why was Hikawa-san carrying this article?

01:10:23.860 --> 01:10:25.240
Wait, this date...

01:10:26.240 --> 01:10:29.830
As I thought. It was the night before Yamao-san's hit-and-run accident!

01:10:30.530 --> 01:10:34.330
That reminds me, at that time...Yamao-san was sitting next to Hikawa-san.

01:10:34.910 --> 01:10:37.080
Which means Yamao-san wasn't looking at the same side we were...But instead at the opposite side.

01:10:37.460 --> 01:10:42.170
In other words, he frowned because he saw this article.

01:10:45.920 --> 01:10:46.880
Could it be...

01:10:51.760 --> 01:10:55.020
Kudou-kun? I lost contact with Tsuburaya-kun and the others.

01:10:55.390 --> 01:10:56.310
What now?

01:10:56.770 --> 01:10:57.440
Also...

01:10:58.560 --> 01:10:59.020
Hello?

01:11:14.090 --> 01:11:16.090
That was the cell phone base station, wasn't it?

01:11:16.760 --> 01:11:20.380
Both of them! Even the landline connection is cut!

01:11:21.050 --> 01:11:23.390
So the base stations for both cell phones and the landlines were...

01:11:23.550 --> 01:11:26.390
Hey, hey, and accident happened right on the day of our ceremony?

01:11:26.680 --> 01:11:28.890
No, this isn't an accident at all!

01:11:29.180 --> 01:11:31.600
Huh? My cell phone isn't connecting...

01:11:31.650 --> 01:11:32.440
It's out of range now...

01:11:32.440 --> 01:11:33.650
Can you hear me, Haibara?

01:11:34.270 --> 01:11:34.900
I can hear you.

01:11:35.440 --> 01:11:36.480
How's the situation over there?

01:11:36.900 --> 01:11:39.990
The cell phones aren't working, so people are in a bit of a panic.

01:11:40.450 --> 01:11:41.030
As I expected.

01:11:41.450 --> 01:11:45.740
And also, about the kids...There were people who saw them with Touma-kun.

01:11:46.830 --> 01:11:49.540
Afterward, the four of them seem to have gone somewhere.

01:11:51.210 --> 01:11:52.620
Come back here immediately!

01:11:53.380 --> 01:11:54.080
Got it!

01:11:54.960 --> 01:11:56.630
Those guys... Don't tell me...

01:12:01.340 --> 01:12:02.680
Does this place look about right?

01:12:03.140 --> 01:12:04.680
Yeah, I think so.

01:12:05.680 --> 01:12:07.310
Hey, you're too noisy!

01:12:12.140 --> 01:12:13.900
How's it? Someone still there?

01:12:18.150 --> 01:12:19.940
Still there!

01:12:20.070 --> 01:12:21.400
Why's this happening!?

01:12:21.950 --> 01:12:23.110
What are you talking about?

01:12:23.490 --> 01:12:24.530
Let's run!

01:12:24.460 --> 01:12:25.170
Good idea!

01:12:26.420 --> 01:12:27.280
Hold on!

01:12:27.670 --> 01:12:29.300
We'll explain later!

01:12:29.500 --> 01:12:31.000
Anyway, please run!

01:12:31.710 --> 01:12:32.830
What's this about!?

01:12:37.380 --> 01:12:38.750
Since when were we being followed?

01:12:39.300 --> 01:12:40.300
No idea!

01:12:40.420 --> 01:12:42.090
By the time we realized, they were already there!

01:12:42.300 --> 01:12:43.340
Some bad person?

01:12:43.840 --> 01:12:45.050
No idea!

01:12:45.260 --> 01:12:46.510
I'm so scared!

01:12:46.600 --> 01:12:48.140
That's why we're running away!

01:12:58.440 --> 01:13:00.940
At that time, I was also running away...

01:13:28.140 --> 01:13:29.220
You hear that?

01:13:29.430 --> 01:13:30.140
Yeah.

01:13:30.430 --> 01:13:32.020
THis is bad. You should wait h--

01:13:32.020 --> 01:13:33.270
There's no way I'm going to wait here!

01:14:04.720 --> 01:14:06.220
Aren't you being a little too forward for a kid?

01:14:06.550 --> 01:14:07.340
Yeah, yeah.

01:14:11.510 --> 01:14:12.600
A cave!

01:14:13.180 --> 01:14:14.310
Let's hide in there!

01:14:15.730 --> 01:14:16.600
Hurry, hurry!

01:14:20.860 --> 01:14:22.070
Wait, you all!

01:14:22.860 --> 01:14:24.400
This is bad! Haibara, they're all yours!

01:14:24.940 --> 01:14:25.320
Got it!

01:14:26.320 --> 01:14:28.530
Geez, those guys...Why'd they have to go in?

01:14:30.410 --> 01:14:31.330
Let's head futher in.

01:14:32.080 --> 01:14:34.200
This goes on for quite a bit!

01:14:34.620 --> 01:14:35.330
Wait!

01:14:35.660 --> 01:14:37.080
Haibara, hurry and get in!

01:14:37.210 --> 01:14:40.040
You shouldn't have come in! Do you want to die here!?

01:14:40.580 --> 01:14:42.840
But adults can't come in here, can they?

01:14:43.000 --> 01:14:48.380
Touma-kun was able to get in, wasn't he? Moreover, what would you do if you were shot from the entrance?

01:14:49.130 --> 01:14:50.050
Geez!

01:14:50.640 --> 01:14:53.560
You guys! Why did you come in here!?

01:14:53.640 --> 01:14:54.560
Just said that.

01:14:55.270 --> 01:14:57.140
Now we have no choice but to go futher in!

01:14:57.390 --> 01:14:58.140
Yep, yep.

01:15:01.360 --> 01:15:03.690
You were running from someone?

01:15:03.980 --> 01:15:06.110
I just remembered that.

01:15:06.490 --> 01:15:09.530
As I thought. I can see the truth now.

01:15:10.450 --> 01:15:12.660
This is bad! If my deduction's correct...

01:15:12.910 --> 01:15:13.620
Hey...

01:15:13.660 --> 01:15:14.450
What's the matter?

01:15:14.870 --> 01:15:18.250
Hurry up! We have to get out of here and reach the dam before the culprit does!

01:15:18.330 --> 01:15:19.290
Something at the dam?

01:15:19.540 --> 01:15:21.080
I have no idea what this is about!

01:15:21.250 --> 01:15:23.250
Please explain properly!

01:15:23.340 --> 01:15:26.590
I don't have any proof yet. It's only my deduction, but...

01:15:27.800 --> 01:15:32.470
The culprit behind all the incidents is... Yamao-san!

01:15:33.720 --> 01:15:36.560
If we assume he broke into a jewelry store in Tokyo 8 years ago...

01:15:36.810 --> 01:15:41.690
Killed the president and made off with jewelry worth one billion yen...

01:15:41.850 --> 01:15:43.360
Everything falls into place.

01:15:44.980 --> 01:15:47.780
Being pursued by loansharks over his debts, Yamao-san...

01:15:48.230 --> 01:15:51.400
Headed for his grandmother's house in his hometown of Kitanosawa Village.

01:15:52.230 --> 01:15:53.360
And on the way there...

01:15:55.230 --> 01:15:57.610
At the entrance of the village, he ran into Natsuki-san.

01:15:58.360 --> 01:15:59.570
Yamao-san panicked.

01:16:00.160 --> 01:16:03.410
If he were caught by the police right then, the murder-robbery would be discovered.

01:16:04.080 --> 01:16:07.000
Not to mention the stolen jewels were still in the car.

01:16:08.210 --> 01:16:13.040
After hitting her, he stopped the car to check on the victim as people normally do.

01:16:13.680 --> 01:16:15.930
As he was looking at Natsuki-san under the cliff...

01:16:16.760 --> 01:16:20.680
Most likely, he was spotted by someone...Toumo-san.

01:16:22.640 --> 01:16:23.480
Me?

01:16:23.940 --> 01:16:28.280
Touma-san, on that day, didn't you go after your mother who had left before dawn?

01:16:28.940 --> 01:16:32.360
You planned to meet her at the hospital so you walked to the scene of the incident.

01:16:32.910 --> 01:16:33.660
That's why...

01:16:35.020 --> 01:16:37.280
Huh? Mommy...

01:16:38.620 --> 01:16:42.120
This is great! I finally get to see Mommy!

01:16:43.170 --> 01:16:46.750
Then, Touma-kun thought that was a continuation of 8 years ago?

01:16:47.130 --> 01:16:52.880
Yeah. It must have been easy for Yamao-san to knock Touma-san out and put him in the car.

01:16:53.630 --> 01:16:55.680
The reason he kept driving..

01:16:55.840 --> 01:16:58.720
was because he couldn't decide what to do with Touma-san.

01:16:58.890 --> 01:17:01.480
But, at that time, his cover had been blown.

01:17:03.690 --> 01:17:07.940
Because Touma-san woke up and witnessed the scattering of the stolen diamonds.

01:17:08.570 --> 01:17:12.650
Then, what he was trying to remember when he saw the diamond dust...

01:17:13.110 --> 01:17:15.070
Was infact the real treasure!

01:17:17.920 --> 01:17:21.590
Since the jewels had been seen, Yamao-san likely decided to take action.

01:17:31.430 --> 01:17:33.310
Were the jewels at his grandma's house?

01:17:33.560 --> 01:17:35.060
He must've hidden them somewhere.

01:17:35.230 --> 01:17:39.100
Right. Yamao-san was checking for the location of the old house.

01:17:40.490 --> 01:17:43.990
He turned himself in because he was sure he would be out in few years.

01:17:44.660 --> 01:17:47.580
However, the punishment was heavier than he thought...

01:17:47.830 --> 01:17:50.460
And in the meantime, the village had sunk to the bottom of the dam.

01:17:51.210 --> 01:17:55.160
In order to retrieve the jewel, he had to somehow drain the water from the dam.

01:17:55.250 --> 01:17:56.050
The water?

01:17:56.210 --> 01:17:57.050
Drain it all?

01:17:57.260 --> 01:17:59.080
That's why he targeted this ceremony.

01:17:59.300 --> 01:18:00.220
Why is that?

01:18:00.720 --> 01:18:03.470
Because the dam personnel would also participate in the ceremony!

01:18:04.200 --> 01:18:08.780
Only two people remain as lookouts. They would never dream of someone blowing it up.

01:18:09.160 --> 01:18:10.830
If he does that, the village will--

01:18:11.200 --> 01:18:12.540
Everyone will die!

01:18:13.290 --> 01:18:15.620
We have to get to the dam before he does!

01:18:15.670 --> 01:18:16.210
Look!

01:18:17.040 --> 01:18:17.790
There's light!

01:18:18.040 --> 01:18:18.840
It's the exit!

01:18:19.140 --> 01:18:21.860
We're out!

01:18:24.210 --> 01:18:25.960
All clear. You guys can come out.

01:18:28.590 --> 01:18:31.380
The discharge conduit. If we go in there...

01:18:34.530 --> 01:18:37.150
No doubt about it. It's the shortest distance.

01:18:41.070 --> 01:18:43.190
Then, the one who killed Hikawa-san was also...

01:18:43.440 --> 01:18:44.780
Yeah, it was Yamao-san.

01:18:46.160 --> 01:18:49.500
On top of carrying out his plan, he had two obstacles to overcome.

01:18:50.290 --> 01:18:51.750
One of them was Hikawa-san.

01:18:52.880 --> 01:18:57.300
As a classmate in the village's branch school and also an insurance investigator....

01:18:57.930 --> 01:19:01.600
He found out that Yamao-san was responsible for the jewelry robbery...

01:19:02.300 --> 01:19:06.850
And of the condition of getting his share of the loot, he offered to help with the crime.

01:19:07.810 --> 01:19:10.600
So if we assume Yamao-san pretended to agree...

01:19:10.850 --> 01:19:14.480
But infact planned to murder Hikawa-san before blowing up the dam...

01:19:14.730 --> 01:19:15.610
Then everything fits.

01:19:16.320 --> 01:19:21.070
It didn't look to me that Hikawa-san was merely blackmailing Yamao-san.

01:19:21.570 --> 01:19:26.620
Moreover, for both the crime of blowing up the dam and killing Hikawa-san...

01:19:26.750 --> 01:19:29.790
The ideal scapegoat would be Mutou-san.

01:19:30.960 --> 01:19:36.300
He made it seems as if it was a crime by Mutou-san who loathed Hikawa-san's betrayal of his hometown as well as the dam project.

01:19:36.800 --> 01:19:40.180
But, how did he talk Hikawa-san into going to that place with him?

01:19:40.630 --> 01:19:42.930
Well, this is just a guess, but...

01:19:43.550 --> 01:19:45.140
What? Mutou did?

01:19:45.720 --> 01:19:48.270
It seems he got wind of our plan...

01:19:48.600 --> 01:19:50.600
And said he wanted to meet up and talk.

01:19:51.100 --> 01:19:53.940
Depending on the situation, we may have to finish him off first.

01:19:55.230 --> 01:19:58.940
He likely said things like that in order to get Hikawa-san willing to take action.

01:19:59.110 --> 01:20:02.820
That's why the two of them walked through the valley and the snowfield, to stay out of people's sight.

01:20:03.530 --> 01:20:05.660
And the other obstacle was-

01:20:05.740 --> 01:20:08.700
that the governor would attend the commemorative ceremony.

01:20:09.460 --> 01:20:13.500
If the governor were coming, the press and related company would naturally come along wih him.

01:20:13.920 --> 01:20:17.880
Even if the base station explosions should disable the cell phones and landlines...

01:20:18.210 --> 01:20:21.090
It'd be unavoidable that news of the dam's breakdown would leak.

01:20:21.430 --> 01:20:22.220
I see.

01:20:22.680 --> 01:20:24.220
Even if he managed to sink the whole village,

01:20:24.300 --> 01:20:28.640
he'd need time afterwards in order to find the location of the hidden gems.

01:20:28.770 --> 01:20:31.520
Therefore, in order to stop the governor from visiting the village...

01:20:31.600 --> 01:20:34.560
And to test his explosives along the way, he blew up the tunnel.

01:20:38.900 --> 01:20:43.700
However...Touma-san returning to consciousness was completely out of his expectation.

01:20:44.660 --> 01:20:49.330
The sheer coincidence of Touma-san having amnesia over the day of the incident was reassuring break for him, but...

01:20:49.750 --> 01:20:53.370
Due to the diamond dust acting as a trigger, his lost memories were on the verge of returning.

01:20:53.960 --> 01:20:56.670
So he figured he would just finish all of you once.

01:20:57.750 --> 01:21:00.210
After he gets the jewels, all he needs to do is take off.

01:21:00.670 --> 01:21:03.050
He should already have a getaway plan in place.

01:21:03.260 --> 01:21:03.840
Yeah.

01:21:04.180 --> 01:21:05.260
What's wrong, Touma?

01:21:06.390 --> 01:21:07.260
Are you tired?

01:21:08.560 --> 01:21:10.560
Did something I said ring a bell?

01:21:10.930 --> 01:21:14.230
Yeah. Somehow, something seems wrong. I wonder what...

01:21:14.900 --> 01:21:17.360
I'm sorry, but right now we have to hurry.

01:21:17.820 --> 01:21:21.150
It took time for Yamao-san to attack Touma-san...

01:21:21.320 --> 01:21:23.610
So he likely hasn't set the bombs on the dam yet.

01:21:24.740 --> 01:21:26.780
Besides that, there are personnel there, right?

01:21:27.780 --> 01:21:29.870
If that's the case, there's still hope.

01:21:30.580 --> 01:21:31.540
Are we there yet?

01:21:31.790 --> 01:21:34.120
Why is it nothing but uphill?

01:21:35.920 --> 01:21:37.130
Come on up!

01:21:41.760 --> 01:21:42.460
Be careful.

01:21:45.220 --> 01:21:46.590
I'm tired...

01:21:48.300 --> 01:21:49.810
Touma, you're nearly there, come on.

01:21:50.100 --> 01:21:52.100
Somehow we managed to get into the dam without trouble.

01:21:52.220 --> 01:21:54.940
eh...It's nothing but trouble!

01:21:56.190 --> 01:21:57.060
Are you alright?

01:21:57.310 --> 01:21:58.270
I'm not...

01:21:58.650 --> 01:22:01.150
I'm so exhausted I can't take another step...

01:22:01.360 --> 01:22:06.320
haha..Guess not...You guy's stay here and protect Touma-san.

01:22:06.740 --> 01:22:09.160
I'll go notify the personnel on lookout.

01:22:10.200 --> 01:22:10.990
Roger.

01:22:11.240 --> 01:22:12.370
Please leave it to us.

01:22:12.870 --> 01:22:16.750
I'll go look for Mutou-san workshed. It should be near here.

01:22:17.250 --> 01:22:18.460
Be careful.

01:22:19.080 --> 01:22:21.420
Yamao-san might have already beat us to it.

01:22:21.550 --> 01:22:22.300
Got it.

01:22:22.960 --> 01:22:24.510
You guys better go hide immediately.

01:22:24.670 --> 01:22:25.800
All right.

01:22:54.870 --> 01:22:55.540
This is!?

01:22:57.830 --> 01:22:59.880
Are you all right? Please hang in there!

01:23:01.380 --> 01:23:04.960
No external injuries...They must've been knocked out with stun gun.

01:23:05.210 --> 01:23:06.720
Wait...

01:23:09.760 --> 01:23:10.470
Don't tell me...

01:23:12.600 --> 01:23:14.680
Those are the same types of bombs from the capital highway!

01:23:15.140 --> 01:23:16.390
damn, how did he...

01:23:17.060 --> 01:23:18.940
Did he get here by car or snowmobile?

01:23:22.770 --> 01:23:23.320
What's up!?

01:23:23.730 --> 01:23:27.070
Kudou-kun... I've reached the worksed, but...This is bad!

01:23:27.400 --> 01:23:29.200
Mutou-san has been knocked out cold!

01:23:29.570 --> 01:23:30.200
As I thought!

01:23:31.200 --> 01:23:33.620
The dam personnel over here are also out cold.

01:23:34.160 --> 01:23:36.410
The stun gun attack likely took them by suprise.

01:23:36.750 --> 01:23:39.710
Wait a minutes...This is strange...

01:23:40.540 --> 01:23:42.290
This is some incredibly fast work...

01:23:46.000 --> 01:23:49.260
Kudou -kun! What happened!? Answer me, Kudou-kun!

01:23:52.430 --> 01:23:53.350
Don't tell me...

01:23:53.600 --> 01:23:54.350
Bombs!?

01:23:54.810 --> 01:23:56.060
You're too loud!

01:23:56.560 --> 01:23:58.890
We only confided in you since you're the famous detective Mouri-san.

01:23:59.230 --> 01:24:01.810
If others hear this, it'll likely result in panic!

01:24:02.060 --> 01:24:04.270
My apologies.

01:24:04.520 --> 01:24:07.740
And? Have they been confirmed to have been time bombs?

01:24:08.360 --> 01:24:11.820
We're received a report that fragments of a timer were found at the scene.

01:24:12.450 --> 01:24:15.530
We're worried about the two guys left at the dam, so we're heading back.

01:24:16.030 --> 01:24:18.200
We can't communicate with them from here, after all.

01:24:18.370 --> 01:24:20.660
Is it possible to use cell phones at the dam?

01:24:20.870 --> 01:24:23.170
If yougo near the dam, you'll see a base station.

01:24:23.670 --> 01:24:26.170
I might be able to call Conan-kun's cell phone.

01:24:26.500 --> 01:24:28.710
Yeah. We'll go as well.

01:24:31.180 --> 01:24:32.260
A gunshot again...

01:24:32.680 --> 01:24:34.550
I wonder Conan-kun is all right?

01:24:34.890 --> 01:24:35.890
I'm worried.

01:24:36.390 --> 01:24:39.730
I can't stand anymore! Let's go too!

01:24:52.860 --> 01:24:54.200
Idiot of a brat!

01:24:54.780 --> 01:25:00.200
If you simply enjoyed the Snow Festival like you were supposed to... You could have died without pain.

01:25:01.040 --> 01:25:03.080
Out with it! Where are you friends?

01:25:03.460 --> 01:25:04.540
I don't have any friends with me...

01:25:04.790 --> 01:25:09.420
Looks like you won't know your place without experiencing some more pain!

01:25:28.320 --> 01:25:30.400
You brat...The nerve of you!

01:25:31.820 --> 01:25:35.030
I don't have time to play with you!

01:25:36.950 --> 01:25:40.080
There ain't much time, so I'll just trust you've really come alone.

01:25:41.500 --> 01:25:45.370
Don't worry. In 15 minutes, when the explosions start...

01:25:45.750 --> 01:25:48.090
Heaven'll immediately become really crowded!

01:25:48.670 --> 01:25:52.630
Farewell...Brat!

01:26:06.600 --> 01:26:07.440
Mizuki-san...

01:26:09.270 --> 01:26:11.860
The gunshot just now sounded different. We have to hurry!

01:26:18.450 --> 01:26:19.490
Hang on!

01:26:19.580 --> 01:26:22.620
You guys! Thank goodness, you're all right!

01:26:22.660 --> 01:26:23.790
Ai chan! Haibara-san! Haibara-san! Haibara!

01:26:25.160 --> 01:26:26.710
Mizuki...Damn you!

01:26:31.750 --> 01:26:33.590
Give it up, Yamao-kun.

01:26:34.800 --> 01:26:36.180
Are you all right, Conan-kun?

01:26:37.840 --> 01:26:39.470
That aside, why are you here?

01:26:39.850 --> 01:26:45.230
Somehow, I had a bad premonition. So i decided to hurry over.

01:26:46.480 --> 01:26:47.230
What about your gun?

01:26:48.770 --> 01:26:53.070
I have license for rifles. I am a good shooter.

01:26:53.570 --> 01:26:55.070
Yeah, it seems that way.

01:26:59.240 --> 01:27:00.410
Look out, Mizuki-san!

01:27:02.700 --> 01:27:04.450
Hand it over, Mizuki!

01:27:21.640 --> 01:27:22.350
Touma-san?

01:27:22.510 --> 01:27:23.100
Hey...

01:27:23.220 --> 01:27:23.890
What's the matter?

01:27:26.270 --> 01:27:29.440
You're the...You're the lady from back then!

01:27:30.060 --> 01:27:32.360
You were wearing glasses before, but there's no doubt about it!

01:27:35.070 --> 01:27:37.740
Sis, you don't understand anything about my dreams at all!

01:27:38.530 --> 01:27:40.410
What're you doing?

01:27:41.490 --> 01:27:44.280
Ouch...Why'd you do that!?

01:27:55.300 --> 01:28:01.010
I see. What Touma-san saw 8 years ago...was Mizuki-san,wasn't it?

01:28:01.720 --> 01:28:04.260
That's why you couldn't follow us into the cave.

01:28:05.100 --> 01:28:07.470
You told Uncle Kogorou yesterday, didn't you?

01:28:07.600 --> 01:28:10.440
I can't stand dark, narrow places...

01:28:12.860 --> 01:28:16.360
Mizuki! What in the world is this about!?

01:28:17.230 --> 01:28:18.070
Conan-kun...

01:28:18.150 --> 01:28:19.950
You mentioned the cave, but...

01:28:20.070 --> 01:28:21.950
Don't tell me!

01:28:22.160 --> 01:28:26.330
Yeah...The person who attacked us earlier was Mizuki-san.

01:28:27.700 --> 01:28:33.040
MIzuki-san was afraid that Touma-san, who witnessed the whole incident, would regain consciousness.

01:28:33.460 --> 01:28:39.880
As such, she began working the front desk of the new village's lodge in front of Touma-san's house....

01:28:40.420 --> 01:28:43.680
And secretly watched over him for 8 years.

01:28:44.510 --> 01:28:46.310
Is that true, Mizuki?

01:28:47.890 --> 01:28:49.890
After touma-san regained consciousness...

01:28:50.430 --> 01:28:54.190
You switch from glasses to contacts and altered hairstyle slightly.

01:28:54.610 --> 01:28:58.070
It was all to prevent Touma-san from recalling who you were should he see your face.

01:28:59.110 --> 01:29:01.400
You made use of Uncle's advice, didn't you?

01:29:02.570 --> 01:29:04.240
I decided to try contact lenses.

01:29:05.780 --> 01:29:10.330
But, it was no avail, as Touma-san's memories gradually began to return, so...

01:29:10.700 --> 01:29:14.670
Before he could completely regain his memories, you thought you'd silence him.

01:29:14.960 --> 01:29:17.670
But, you're one mean elder sister.

01:29:18.130 --> 01:29:20.550
To thrust your younger sister in front of a car.

01:29:22.880 --> 01:29:24.970
I never meant to kill her!

01:29:27.760 --> 01:29:31.140
I only wanted to make her fall and hurt her a little...

01:29:31.600 --> 01:29:36.610
But, I didn't know Yamao-kun's car would happen to pass by exactly where my sister had fallen.

01:29:39.270 --> 01:29:42.240
If anyone found out, I wouldn't be able to stay here anymore.

01:29:43.200 --> 01:29:44.990
When I thought of that, I was so afraid...

01:29:45.530 --> 01:29:47.660
By the time I realized it, I had already grabbed my gun.

01:29:48.410 --> 01:29:51.870
But...But I just wanted to keep Touma-kun away from me...

01:29:52.370 --> 01:29:56.380
That's why...I really never intended to kill anyone!

01:29:58.290 --> 01:30:05.050
I know. I know Mizuki-san never intended to hurt anyone.

01:30:07.300 --> 01:30:10.560
Because, If she had the skilled to shoot through yamao-san's shoulder from that distance,

01:30:10.890 --> 01:30:14.100
and to accurately send the dropped gun flying...

01:30:14.440 --> 01:30:17.190
We definitely would have been shot.

01:30:20.690 --> 01:30:23.780
I'm sorry...I'm sorry...

01:30:25.070 --> 01:30:27.450
But, isn't it great, Mizuki?

01:30:28.740 --> 01:30:29.410
With this,

01:30:29.700 --> 01:30:34.580
you can finally be freed from the 8 years of continous torment brought about by that nightmare.

01:30:35.160 --> 01:30:38.830
Thanks to that, I also got to see your pretty face without being covered by glasses.

01:30:42.000 --> 01:30:42.960
Mutou-kun...

01:30:43.460 --> 01:30:47.970
Well' I'll be waiting patiently.

01:30:48.180 --> 01:30:49.180
For you to return here. Always.

01:30:58.480 --> 01:31:01.190
Edogawa-kun! The light is blinking!

01:31:01.520 --> 01:31:01.940
What!?

01:31:10.660 --> 01:31:12.160
Damn it, back then...

01:31:17.120 --> 01:31:19.880
Yamao-san said we had 15 minutes. Damn!

01:31:20.580 --> 01:31:22.750
Everyone, run for it! It's gonna explode!

01:31:25.090 --> 01:31:27.380
Stop wasting time! Hurry!

01:31:34.470 --> 01:31:35.720
Touma, hurry!

01:31:40.440 --> 01:31:41.190
Ayumi-chan!

01:31:41.270 --> 01:31:42.360
Don't stop, keep going!

01:31:42.560 --> 01:31:43.900
You all right? Run!

01:31:45.440 --> 01:31:48.240
This is bad. If the explosions continue at this rate...

01:31:48.530 --> 01:31:49.700
The whole dam will collapse!

01:32:03.340 --> 01:32:07.510
No good...that sound...It's the sound of the outer walls crumbling!

01:32:09.720 --> 01:32:10.720
If I don't do something...

01:32:11.550 --> 01:32:13.390
The collapse will only be a matter of time!

01:32:13.970 --> 01:32:15.640
If all the water flows out from the dam at once...

01:32:16.270 --> 01:32:18.140
The village will be completely destroyed!

01:32:18.810 --> 01:32:21.650
Is there...Is there nothing that can be done to save the village!?

01:32:22.100 --> 01:32:25.070
ah...The ski area...

01:32:33.370 --> 01:32:34.410
Is anyone hurt?

01:32:34.870 --> 01:32:36.080
Is everyone here?

01:32:36.410 --> 01:32:37.620
Conan isn't here!

01:32:38.330 --> 01:32:40.160
There's a boy who's missing!

01:32:40.330 --> 01:32:41.120
What!?

01:32:41.580 --> 01:32:44.290
I think he went missing after he saved me!

01:32:44.790 --> 01:32:45.540
Conan-kun...

01:32:46.040 --> 01:32:47.090
What are you doing?

01:32:56.350 --> 01:32:58.720
What!? There are still bombs left?

01:33:04.350 --> 01:33:05.190
Damn!

01:33:06.690 --> 01:33:08.150
No good. The dam's collapsing!

01:33:08.320 --> 01:33:09.900
Everyone, please stay back!

01:33:09.940 --> 01:33:11.740
No! Conan-kun is still--!

01:33:11.860 --> 01:33:13.950
Until Conan-kun comes, we won't move!

01:33:14.160 --> 01:33:15.320
Conan!

01:33:15.620 --> 01:33:17.280
What are you doing, Kudou-kun!?

01:33:36.890 --> 01:33:37.930
Awesome!

01:33:38.060 --> 01:33:40.060
Go, Conan!

01:33:40.600 --> 01:33:41.430
Where he's going?

01:33:42.560 --> 01:33:44.690
He intends to stop the flood!

01:33:51.040 --> 01:33:53.550
Too reckless! There's no way a kid can do it!

01:33:53.750 --> 01:33:55.670
If he gets caught up in it, he won't have a chance!

01:33:55.880 --> 01:33:56.630
He can do it!

01:33:57.420 --> 01:33:58.760
Conan can do it!

01:33:58.970 --> 01:34:01.430
Nothing is impossible for the Detective Boys!

01:34:03.890 --> 01:34:06.060
It's all up to you... Kudou-kun...

01:34:11.580 --> 01:34:14.920
If I recall, there should be an unused ski area just in front of the village.

01:34:15.920 --> 01:34:17.380
If I use the deep snow,

01:34:17.670 --> 01:34:19.000
maybe it'll work!

01:34:23.340 --> 01:34:24.890
What the hell is that!?

01:34:25.180 --> 01:34:27.720
This is bad! The dam is...

01:34:28.140 --> 01:34:29.260
It's dangerous! We hafta retreat!

01:34:34.940 --> 01:34:37.190
Damn...At this rate, I can't make it in time!

01:34:37.610 --> 01:34:39.520
It's risky, but I'll have to go through the forest!

01:35:03.590 --> 01:35:04.550
Good...

01:35:06.640 --> 01:35:07.640
That was close!

01:35:22.990 --> 01:35:25.610
Damn! Come on, just hang in there a bit longer!

01:35:36.290 --> 01:35:40.250
Hey! If all the water comes down at once, what'll happen to the village?

01:35:40.750 --> 01:35:42.210
It'll be really bad!

01:35:42.340 --> 01:35:43.880
We don't know how bad it'll be!

01:35:44.090 --> 01:35:47.340
Without a doubt...The whole village is gonna sink!

01:35:48.510 --> 01:35:50.430
No way...

01:36:01.770 --> 01:36:02.320
I can see it!

01:36:10.620 --> 01:36:11.450
Conan-kun!

01:36:14.200 --> 01:36:15.910
That kid...What's he up to now?

01:36:25.090 --> 01:36:29.010
An avalanche! He's planning to start an avalanche to change the flow of the water!

01:36:32.300 --> 01:36:33.470
Conan-kun!

01:36:39.480 --> 01:36:40.900
Damn! Not now!

01:36:43.110 --> 01:36:43.940
Conan-kun!

01:36:44.520 --> 01:36:45.230
No!

01:36:45.980 --> 01:36:51.620
Shit...Shit...Shit, shit, shit!

01:36:52.370 --> 01:36:53.910
SHIT!

01:37:14.600 --> 01:37:15.510
Not good!

01:37:17.100 --> 01:37:18.850
That brat...Freaking did it...

01:37:18.980 --> 01:37:20.060
Run!

01:37:24.650 --> 01:37:25.570
Please make it in time!

01:37:29.570 --> 01:37:30.400
LOOK OUT!

01:37:38.250 --> 01:37:39.040
Ran..

01:37:47.130 --> 01:37:49.010
Conan-kun...

01:38:19.790 --> 01:38:20.750
Conan-kun...

01:38:22.870 --> 01:38:27.880
Conan! Where are you? Conan... You there!?

01:38:29.130 --> 01:38:32.630
I can hear everyone's voices...

01:38:33.840 --> 01:38:36.300
Looks like they avoided getting caught in this...

01:38:37.220 --> 01:38:39.220
I have to get out of here too or else...

01:38:41.980 --> 01:38:44.770
This is bad...I can't move...

01:38:45.270 --> 01:38:49.400
Gotta...Gotta do something...

01:38:50.070 --> 01:38:53.780
Conan-kun! Conan-kun... Conan-kun... Conan-kun!

01:38:54.150 --> 01:38:57.490
(Conan.. Conan... Conan...)

01:38:57.490 --> 01:38:59.370
Brat... Brat!

01:38:59.580 --> 01:39:01.910
How many minutes!? How many minutes have passed!?

01:39:02.450 --> 01:39:03.120
It was...

01:39:03.160 --> 01:39:04.120
11 minutes and 50 seconds.

01:39:05.080 --> 01:39:07.960
It's been almost 12 minutes since the avalanche occurred!

01:39:08.090 --> 01:39:09.040
What'd you say!?

01:39:09.130 --> 01:39:10.090
That means...

01:39:10.130 --> 01:39:13.050
We have only 3 minutes until the 15-minute golden time is stop!

01:39:13.590 --> 01:39:14.420
No way!

01:39:15.010 --> 01:39:16.680
Everyone! Help them find Edogawa-kun!

01:39:17.680 --> 01:39:18.930
Don't tell me, Conan-kun was...

01:39:19.600 --> 01:39:20.810
Caught in the avalanche!?

01:39:24.810 --> 01:39:26.940
Please... Go through!

01:39:31.280 --> 01:39:31.980
It went through!

01:39:33.400 --> 01:39:34.740
Everyone, keep quiet!

01:39:35.650 --> 01:39:37.950
Listen carefully for the kid's cell phone!

01:39:44.250 --> 01:39:47.170
Conan-kun, where...Where are you?

01:39:52.590 --> 01:39:53.170
There!

01:39:53.420 --> 01:39:54.670
What now!?

01:39:54.720 --> 01:39:57.010
Conan-kun! Where!?

01:39:57.240 --> 01:39:59.780
Conan!

01:40:05.980 --> 01:40:07.730
Found it! Conan-kun's cell phone!

01:40:11.480 --> 01:40:14.320
Please... Please come out, Conan-kun!

01:40:14.510 --> 01:40:17.180
Over here! Comb through every inch of this area!

01:40:17.930 --> 01:40:21.520
Conan-kun! Conan-kun!

01:40:24.600 --> 01:40:27.310
Damn! Not here either?

01:40:27.730 --> 01:40:28.820
No...No way...

01:40:28.940 --> 01:40:31.360
Conan-kun, where... Where are you!?

01:40:31.820 --> 01:40:33.700
Please, come out!

01:40:34.240 --> 01:40:35.320
Your hands are bleeding!

01:40:35.580 --> 01:40:38.660
Why? Why aren't you here!? Conan-kun!

01:40:40.870 --> 01:40:43.160
Conan-kun...Will we ever see him again...?

01:40:45.500 --> 01:40:49.380
Once you sever your ties, you might not see each other ever again.

01:40:50.880 --> 01:40:51.670
No way...

01:40:51.670 --> 01:40:53.470
You're kidding, right...?

01:40:53.840 --> 01:40:57.050
Conan-kun...You can't die!

01:40:57.890 --> 01:41:00.220
Less than one minute until the time limit!

01:41:01.770 --> 01:41:02.430
Ran...

01:41:03.560 --> 01:41:04.480
Don't give up!

01:41:04.520 --> 01:41:05.640
What's wrong, Ran?

01:41:08.270 --> 01:41:09.310
Shinichi...

01:41:13.610 --> 01:41:16.820
Please... If you're nearby...

01:41:18.280 --> 01:41:21.290
If you're somewhere close, please help...

01:41:22.120 --> 01:41:24.330
Help us, Shinichi!

01:41:25.120 --> 01:41:30.130
(Shinichi...Shinichi...Shinichi...Shinichi...)

01:41:39.680 --> 01:41:41.050
That was Ran's voice...

01:41:42.010 --> 01:41:44.390
I have to tell her where I am...

01:41:55.360 --> 01:41:55.990
Uh...That's...

01:41:56.200 --> 01:41:57.200
A soccer ball!

01:41:57.740 --> 01:41:58.450
Don't tell me!

01:41:59.320 --> 01:42:04.330
Conan-kun...

01:42:11.290 --> 01:42:12.000
Conan-kun!

01:42:13.630 --> 01:42:15.260
He's here! Over here!

01:42:15.300 --> 01:42:17.840
Conan-kun... Hang on, Conan-kun!

01:42:22.720 --> 01:42:26.930
Please, Conan-kun...Open your eyes!

01:42:28.060 --> 01:42:29.520
Conan-kun!

01:42:33.440 --> 01:42:35.900
uh...

01:42:36.490 --> 01:42:37.280
Conan-kun!

01:42:37.820 --> 01:42:40.360
Ran...neechan...

01:42:41.490 --> 01:42:45.200
Thank goodness...Thank goodness, Conan-kun...

01:42:45.290 --> 01:42:46.950
All right!

01:42:50.040 --> 01:42:52.420
As usual, he's a though guy.

01:47:14.970 --> 01:47:19.890
The following afternoon...From the backyard of Yamao-san's previous home that had sunk to the bottom of the dam...

01:47:20.350 --> 01:47:22.980
A suitcase full of gems and jewelry was recovered.

01:47:24.360 --> 01:47:29.360
Presented with the solid evidence, Yamao-san confessed to everything. And thus, the case was solve.

01:47:30.700 --> 01:47:33.820
Mizuki-san confessed to what she did to her sister 8 years ago.

01:47:34.320 --> 01:47:36.580
She would face police questioning.

01:47:37.540 --> 01:47:41.290
As for Touma-kun, he hadn't yet regained the entirely of his memory.

01:47:41.830 --> 01:47:42.790
But...

01:47:43.080 --> 01:47:49.550
for the time when he recalls everything...And showcases the smile he originally had...One needs not wait too long.

01:47:53.470 --> 01:47:56.430
About your baggage, I have scheduled a delivery to this address.

01:47:56.810 --> 01:47:59.390
Thank you very much. We're grateful for everything.

01:47:59.890 --> 01:48:03.400
Although things turned out this way...Please still feel free to come again!

01:48:03.690 --> 01:48:04.270
Yes!

01:48:04.060 --> 01:48:04.610
(We'll come again!)

01:48:04.980 --> 01:48:05.690
We'll definitely come!

01:48:10.190 --> 01:48:12.570
Hey, you guys, hurry up already!

01:48:13.070 --> 01:48:14.570
If you mess about, I'm gonna leave you here!

01:48:15.200 --> 01:48:17.450
Why's your dad in such a hurry?

01:48:18.410 --> 01:48:21.500
I haven't bought a souvenir for Makoto-san!

01:48:21.960 --> 01:48:22.960
Me neither!

01:48:23.790 --> 01:48:26.080
Hold it, you guys! We don't have that sort of time!

01:48:28.130 --> 01:48:31.170
That reminds me... What was it I needed to buy?

01:48:31.880 --> 01:48:35.340
We also haven't finished buying a souvenir for Kobayashi-sensei!

01:48:35.680 --> 01:48:37.680
It was the bear buns, right?

01:48:37.930 --> 01:48:41.180
What are you talking about? It's been decided she's getting the mug with swans!

01:48:41.390 --> 01:48:42.890
I think the owl is nicer.

01:48:43.520 --> 01:48:44.900
Huh, aren't those...

01:48:45.310 --> 01:48:48.980
If it's too much of a hassle, why not get everything? It's the professor's money anyway.

01:48:49.190 --> 01:48:49.690
Hey, hey...

01:48:50.400 --> 01:48:54.070
I see. It was the kids who wrote this.

01:48:55.200 --> 01:48:57.450
You guys, hurry up if you're gonna buy some souvenirs!

01:48:57.870 --> 01:49:02.580
Hustle up! If we don't hurry home, I won't be able to catch Yoko-chan's drama!

01:49:03.080 --> 01:49:05.870
Only 15 minutes! I'm driving out in 15 minutes!

01:49:06.110 --> 01:49:08.000
No way!

01:49:08.320 --> 01:49:09.210
Let's hurry!

01:49:12.000 --> 01:49:14.510
Geez, a quarter-hour again?
